{"raw": {"https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11321": {"title": "Adjunct, Department of Elementary Education", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjunct, Department of Elementary Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjunct, Department of Elementary Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis as instructional and supervisory needs arise. The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development welcomes applications from individuals committed to excellence in teaching, mentoring, supervision, and professional preparation. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1,683/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjunct, Department of Elementary Education Department Name Elementary Education Department Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Feinstein School of Education and Human Development Position Overview The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development ( FSEHD ) at Rhode Island College prepares educators, counselors, school psychologists, wellness and exercise science, and youth development professionals who positively impact schools, communities, and the lives of children, youth, and adults. The FSEHD is committed to excellence, equity, inclusion, community engagement, and preparing highly qualified professionals throughout Rhode Island and beyond. The FSEHD invites applications from qualified professionals interested in serving as adjunct faculty teaching content, practicum, or seminar courses and/or supervising student teachers or interns across its undergraduate and graduate programs. Essential Duties Department of Elementary Education \u2013 Programs: Elementary Education undergraduate Program Elementary Education MAT graduate Program Reading Specialist Program Early Childhood Undergraduate Program Early Childhood Undergraduate Certificate Program \u2013 Bilingual Spanish/English Assignments may include: Teaching undergraduate or graduate content courses. Teaching practicum, internship, or seminar courses. Serving as a college supervisor. Supervising student teachers or interns in PK-12 settings or counseling, youth development, or wellness and exercise community organizations. Contact: Karen Capraro, Chair of the Elementary Education Department Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Dean of the FSEHD . Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree. Relevant professional experience in the field. Experience working with diverse learners and communities. Strong communication, mentoring, and supervisory skills. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate Degree preferred. Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00065 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available Multiple Anticipated Start Date or Semester Posting Date 07/07/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis as instructional and supervisory needs arise. The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development welcomes applications from individuals committed to excellence in teaching, mentoring, supervision, and professional preparation. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11267": {"title": "Director of Professional Studies and Continuing Education", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Director of Professional Studies and Continuing Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Director of Professional Studies and Continuing Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00844 Position Title Director of Professional Studies and Continuing Education Division Academic Affairs Division Department Name Professional Studies and Continuing Education Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview Rhode Island College seeks a dynamic and strategic leader to serve as Director of Professional Studies and Continuing Education ( PSCE ). The Director advances the College\u2019s mission by leading innovative continuing, professional, online, adult, and workforce education programs that respond to the evolving needs of the region, with particular attention to unemployed, underemployed, adult, and underserved learners. Reporting to the Vice Provost for Academic Affairs, the Director provides leadership for the planning, administration, and financial management of PSCE programs on campus and at the Workforce Development Hub in Central Falls. The position oversees continuing education programming; manages budgets, grants, contracts, and personnel; and builds strong partnerships with academic departments, campus offices, employers, and community organizations. The Director plays a critical role in expanding access, launching new initiatives, and strengthening Rhode Island College\u2019s impact in workforce and community education. Primary Purpose The Director serves to ensure that the Office of Professional Studies and Continuing Education ( PSCE ) programming aligns with and extends the mission of Rhode Island College ( RIC ) to meet the professional development, continuing, online education, adult education, workforce development and training needs of all sectors of the community and workforce including underemployed, unemployed, and underserved students. The Director reports to the Vice Provost for Academic Affairs and is responsible for the strategic leadership, administration, and financial management of PSCE programs and operations on campus and at the Workforce Development Hub in Central Falls in cooperation with senior administrators and staff, campus partners and support offices, and community and industry partners. Areas of administration and financial management include primary responsibility for most Continuing Education (CE) programs; assistance with the development, funding, staffing, delivery, assessment, and reporting on all programming; and the leadership of PSCE strategic planning and assistance with the implementation of new PSCE and RIC initiatives. Essential Duties Direct administration and management of PSCE department, agency, grant and contract training budgets including expenditures, programming cost estimates and controls, and internal and external budget reporting, and invoicing for contract programming. Lead the development of annual PSCE budget and programming budget forecasts and final annual fiscal year report summary data and analysis of budgets and programs. Manage the administration of PSCE Management Information Services ( MIS ) functions to ensure student and program access and support for all PSCE educational and training programs. Lead the development and submission of all grant and programming proposals with internal offices and external partners. Oversee PSCE hiring and payrolls for college monthly employees, instructional and support services staff, and student employees. Coordinate dual enrollment and concurrent enrollment partnerships and related external engagement activities in collaboration with academic departments, external partners, and relevant college offices. Manage prior learning assessment-related processes, in collaboration with Academic Affairs and other relevant college offices. Coordinate payroll, contracting, and related administrative processes for Summer Sessions and Early Spring programming, in collaboration with relevant academic and administrative offices. Oversee the preparation and authorization of training contracts and memoranda of agreement/understanding with external partners and internal administrators. Oversee and administer CE cohort courses and programs eligible for Group-Level scholarship incentive rates. Track PSCE education and training courses and enrollments and provide monthly and annual course and section enrollment reports. Lead the development and implementation of PSCE\u2019s annual marketing plan and provide additional marketing assistance for individual PSCE programs as needed. Advance the development and support of PSCE campus, community and corporate programs, and other externally facing educational partnerships with internal and external partners. Represent PSCE on campus committees that address administrative and business processes, upgrades, and changes. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Vice Provost for Academic Affairs. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Demonstrated leadership and supervisory ability in complex programmatic and administrative settings. Knowledge of trends, issues, and accepted practices relevant to the position. Excellent interpersonal skills, including the ability to relate to and work cooperatively with various groups of people. Excellent written and verbal communications skills including the ability to communicate with a diverse community both internally and externally. Ability to think creatively about solutions to problems. Required Qualifications Education: Master\u2019s Degree Experience: Five years of managerial experience and program development at the college/university level. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate. Prior administrative experience in continuing education. Prior experience developing and delivering continuing education, adult education and workforce development courses and certificate programs. Multilingual preferred. Does this position have Direct Reports? Yes Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 15NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $90,000-$110,000 Work Schedule Full-Time Monday-Friday 8:30 AM \u2013 4:30 PM Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Vice Provost for Academic Affairs Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Continuing End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit PSA Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 05/11/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned master\u2019s degree? yes no * Do you have five year's of managerial experience and program development at the college/university level? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11386": {"title": "Electrician", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Electrician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Electrician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. At time of appointment, applicant must be physically qualified to perform assigned duties as evidenced by a physician\u2019s certificate. Upon hire, candidate may be required to arrange for an official transcript of highest degree earned to be mailed/transmitted directly from the institution to RIC. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Information Position Information Posting Number CS00637 Position Title Electrician Division Administration and Finance Division Department Name Maintenance and Repairs Position Type Staff \u2013 Classified General Statement of Duties To install, inspect, maintain, alter and repair electrical lines, equipment and apparatus; and to do related work as required. Supervision Received Receives work assignments from a superior with considerable latitude for the use of independent judgement in the application of the practices and techniques of the trade; work is reviewed usually upon completion for satisfactory performance. Supervision Exercised As required, supervises the work of helpers or others assigned to assist. Position Overview The Electrician is responsible for installing, inspecting, maintaining, altering, and repairing electrical systems, equipment, and apparatus throughout Rhode Island College facilities. The position performs skilled electrical work involving wiring, cables, power equipment, machinery, lighting, communication and signaling systems, and other electrical and electronic equipment. The Electrician works with considerable independence and judgment in applying established trade practices and techniques, including the ability to read and work from electrical diagrams and blueprints and safely handle high-voltage systems. The position may also perform preventive maintenance, troubleshooting, minor repairs, and related work on motors, generators, appliances, and specialized equipment, and may supervise helpers or other employees assigned to assist with electrical work. A current Rhode Island journeyman electrician\u2019s license is required and must be maintained as a condition of employment. Illustrative Examples of Work Performed To install, inspect, maintain, alter and repair electric wires and cables (including those carrying high voltages), power appliances, machinery, overhead circuits, underground conduits and pole lines. To install, inspect and repair special medical equipment such as X-ray and physiotherapy equipment. To install, inspect, regulate and repair all types of electrical traffic control signals. At a state institution, to repair and maintain various types of electrical equipment, such as refrigerators, stoves, elevators and dairy and laundry machinery. As assigned, to install, operate, maintain and repair various electrical equipment and apparatus at the Veterans\u2019 Memorial Building or any other state facility involving stage or theatrical presentations including lighting control and lighting contact boards, public address systems and thermostatically controlled heating and ventilating units. To inspect, make minor repairs to, clean and oil motors and generators. To install, inspect and maintain communication, signaling and other electronic systems. To regulate and repair electric master and secondary clocks. To do related work as required. Education Such as may have been gained through the completion of ten school grades. Experience Such as may have been gained through employment as a journeyman electrician. Or Combination of Education and Experience Any combination of education and experience that shall be substantially equivalent to the above education and experience. Additional Required Qualifications Must possess a journeyman electrician\u2019s license issued by the Rhode Island State Board of Examiners of Electricians and must maintain such licensure as a condition of employment. Knowledges Skills and Capacities A thorough knowledge of the principles, practices, techniques, tools, equipment and materials used in the electrician trade and skill in their application; a working knowledge of safety codes enforced by the State; the ability to read and work from electrical wiring diagrams and blueprints; the ability to handle high voltage wires; the ability to understand and to follow oral and written directions; and related capacities and abilities Preferred Qualifications N/A Position Details FLSA Non-Exempt Full Time / Part Time Full-time Work Schedule 40 Weekly Hours Monday \u2013 Friday 7:00AM \u2013 3:30PM Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Associate Director of Facilities & Operations, Maintenance & Repairs Position Status Permanent - C End of Restricted or Limited Position Civil Service List No Union Code classified Salary Grade 328CA Minimum Salary for Grade $73,210 Maximum Salary for Grade $82,203 Added Salary for This Position N/A Collective Bargaining Unit Council 94 Local 2878 Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Anticipated Start Date 08/15/2026 Application Open Date Application Close Date Special Instructions At time of appointment, applicant must be physically qualified to perform assigned duties as evidenced by a physician\u2019s certificate. Upon hire, candidate may be required to arrange for an official transcript of highest degree earned to be mailed/transmitted directly from the institution to RIC . Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement As an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity institution which values and is committed to expanding the diversity of its faculty and staff, the College invites members of protected classes, including minorities and persons with disabilities, to identify themselves as such at the time of application. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you possess a journeyman electrician\u2019s license issued by the Rhode Island State Board of Examiners of Electricians? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11149": {"title": "Director, Project Management Office", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Director, Project Management Office Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Director, Project Management Office Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00871 Position Title Director, Project Management Office Division Administration and Finance Division Department Name Administration and Finance Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview Rhode Island College is seeking an experienced and strategic leader to establish and lead its Project Management Office ( PMO ) within the Division of Administration and Finance. This is an exciting opportunity to build a PMO from the ground up, shaping the college\u2019s approach to project governance, portfolio management, and organizational transformation. The Director of the Project Management Office will drive the successful delivery of high-impact, cross-functional initiatives by implementing best-in-class project management practices, fostering collaboration across administrative and technology teams, and ensuring projects align with the College\u2019s strategic priorities. Working closely with executive leadership, including the Assistant CIO and senior administrators, the Director will provide portfolio oversight, strengthen institutional project management capabilities, and promote a culture of accountability, transparency, and continuous improvement. Ideal candidates are collaborative leaders with a proven track record of building PMOs, managing complex project portfolios, and leading enterprise-wide initiatives in dynamic, matrixed organizations. This role offers the opportunity to make a lasting institutional impact by improving how projects are planned, prioritized, and delivered across Rhode Island College. Primary Purpose The Director of the Project Management Office ( PMO ) is responsible for establishing, leading and sustaining the PMO within Administration and Finance at the college. This role is responsible for developing governance frameworks, standardizing project management practices, and overseeing the institutional project portfolio to ensure initiatives are delivered on time, within scope, and aligned with strategic priorities. The Director builds and drives the adoption of consistent tools, processes, and delivery standards across a complex organization, while fostering a strong project management culture through coaching, training, and stakeholder engagement. This position serves as the central point of accountability for portfolio transparency, delivery performance, and the ongoing enhancement of project management capabilities across the college. Essential Duties Design, implement, and maintain a Project Management Office framework for the Division of Administration and Finance, establishing governance standards, delivery methodologies, and operating practices aligned with institutional needs and industry best practices. Define and standardize project governance processes across the division, including intake, prioritization, resource planning, risk management, status reporting, and post-implementation review. Build and manage the college\u2019s project portfolio ensuring initiatives are prioritized, resourced, and delivering measurable value. Serve as hands-on project and program manager for complex, cross-functional initiatives, providing direct delivery leadership from initiation through closeout across any functional area within the division. Develop and maintain a portfolio dashboard and reporting cadence that provides division leadership with timely, accurate visibility into project status, risks, dependencies, and outcomes. Facilitate the development of project charters, scope documents, work plans, RACI matrices, and communication plans in partnership with project sponsors and functional area leaders. Partner with the Assistant CIO on IT transformation and enterprise technology initiatives, co-leading delivery on complex programs. Serve as the integration point between stakeholders, proactively identifying and resolving cross-functional dependencies, resource conflicts, and sequencing issues. Champion a project management culture across the college through coaching, mentoring, and targeted training for staff at all levels. Lead the evaluation, selection, and administration of project management tools and platforms, ensuring consistent adoption and use across the college portfolio. Develop and maintain resource capacity models to support data-driven decisions on project prioritization, staffing, and scheduling. Manage vendor and partner relationships on projects, monitoring deliverables, timelines, and contractual performance. Ensure all projects comply with institutional policies, applicable regulations, and relevant security and compliance standards. Provide the college\u2019s Leadership Team with regular portfolio health reports and strategic progress updates, escalating issues requiring executive attention. Supervise and develop PMO staff as the PMO function grows. Occasional Duties Perform other duties as assigned. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Demonstrated experience building a Project Management Office in a complex, multi-function organization. Proven ability to manage a diverse portfolio of concurrent projects. Strong working knowledge of project management methodologies including waterfall, agile, and hybrid approaches, with the judgment to apply the right method to the right initiative. Experience serving as hands-on project and program manager for large, cross-functional enterprise or administrative initiatives. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to prepare and present portfolio-level reports to VP and executive-level audiences. Strong analytical skills with demonstrated experience building and maintaining portfolio dashboards, metrics, and reporting frameworks. Proficiency with project management tools and platforms (e.g., Smartsheet, Jira, MS Project, or equivalent). Exceptional organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage competing priorities across multiple functional domains under deadline pressure. Proven ability to build relationships and foster collaboration across diverse stakeholder groups without direct line authority. Sufficient familiarity with information technology systems and infrastructure to collaborate effectively with IT leadership and manage technology-related projects within the portfolio. High degree of professional integrity and commitment to confidentiality across sensitive administrative domains. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Project Management, Information Systems, Business Administration, or a related field. Experience: Minimum of sevenyears of progressive project management experience; a minimum of three years managing a project portfolio or PMO function, with at least two years in a management or director-level role. Certification: Project Management Professional ( PMP ) certification Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Project Management, Business Administration, Public Administration, Information Systems, or a related field. Additional Project Management certifications (e.g., PMI - ACP , Lean Six Sigma, ITIL ) strongly preferred. Experience in higher education or a public sector environment, with an understanding of the governance, compliance, and stakeholder complexity these settings involve. Demonstrated experience managing projects across multiple administrative functions \u2014 such as finance systems, HRIS , facilities, or enterprise IT \u2014 within a single portfolio. Experience supporting the delivery of enterprise administrative system implementations ( ERP , SIS , HRIS , Finance platforms). Demonstrated experience coaching and mentoring staff at varying levels of project management maturity across non-technical and technical teams. Does this position have Direct Reports? Yes Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 17NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $145,000 - $155,000 Work Schedule Monday \u2013 Friday 8:30AM-4:30PM May require evening and weekend work as needed. Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Assistant Vice President, Financial Operations Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Continuing End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit Non-union Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 08/03/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have a Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Project Management, Information Systems, Business Administration, or a related field? Yes No Do you have a Project Management Professional (PMP) certification? Yes No Do you have a minimum of seven years of progressive project management experience, a minimum of three years managing a project portfolio or PMO function, with at least two years in a management or director-level role? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/10980": {"title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor Operations Management", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Assistant/Associate/Professor Operations Management Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Assistant/Associate/Professor Operations Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates who have an earned master\u2019s degree or equivalent and are pursuing a terminal degree but who have not yet completed their terminal degree by the date of appointment may be considered for appointment at the rank of instructor. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Upon hire, candidate will be required to arrange for an official transcript of highest degree earned to be mailed/transmitted directly from the institution to RIC. Candidates will be prompted during the application process to provide 3 names and email addresses for reference letters. Position Information Position Information Posting Number F00281 Position Title Assistant/Associate/Professor Operations Management Division Academic Affairs Division Department Name School of Business Position Type Faculty Position Overview The IACBE -accredited School of Business at Rhode Island College invites applications for an open-rank, tenure-track faculty position in Operations Management. The successful candidate will teach a variety of operations and management-related courses, including operations management, project management, supply chain management, process management, service operations, and quality assurance, with possible opportunities to teach additional management courses. Essential Duties The IACBE -accredited School of Business at Rhode Island College invites applications for one open rank, tenure-track faculty position (assistant, associate, or full) with a primary focus in Operations Management. We seek candidates with a strong interest in teaching within a liberal arts setting who are eager to teach various operations management courses, including operations management, project management, supply chain management, process management, service operation management, and quality assurance. There may also be opportunities to teach other courses in the broad management area. Successful candidates will be expected to teach three courses in the fall and spring terms (3-3 load). The classes are small, allowing for more student interaction. The college has an average student-to-faculty ratio of 14:1, and most class sizes range between 10 and 30 students. Faculty are also required to advise up to 30 students, which requires guiding students through their management programs. Faculty are also expected to engage in scholarly research leading to publication in peer-reviewed journals and conduct service. The college requires that all applicants and employees be able to perform the above essential duties of the job and will explore reasonable accommodations for individuals with documented disabilities in accordance with ADA requirements. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Department Chair. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Good teaching skills, Good knowledge of operations management (including project management, process management, service management, and supply chain management) The ability and enthusiasm to impart this knowledge to undergraduate students, A willingness to work collegially with other faculty in the School of Business Required Qualifications Ph.D. or D.B.A. in Operations Management or related field, or ABD with a credible plan to complete dissertation within 2 years. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience at the college level. Industry experience in an asset. Interest in teaching and researching Ability to teach in-person, hybrid, or online as directed by the chair and/or dean of the School of Business. Bilingual Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Compensation Benefits Full-time employee benefits include: Comprehensive Health Benefits and Rewards for Wellness Incentives Generous Paid Time Off Family/Parental Leave Tuition Waivers at RIC , CCRI & URI Retirement Plan Long-term Disability Coverage Variety of voluntary add-on\u2019s For a complete listing, visit: http://www.employeebenefits.ri.gov/benefits/new/index.php Reports to (Title) Academic or Calendar Year Academic Position Status Continuing Tenure Track End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit RIC/AFT Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Posting Date 09/24/2024 Application Closing Date Special Instructions Candidates who have an earned master\u2019s degree or equivalent and are pursuing a terminal degree but who have not yet completed their terminal degree by the date of appointment may be considered for appointment at the rank of instructor. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Upon hire, candidate will be required to arrange for an official transcript of highest degree earned to be mailed/transmitted directly from the institution to RIC . Candidates will be prompted during the application process to provide 3 names and email addresses for reference letters. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you hold a Ph.D. or DBA in Operations Management or related field OR ABD with credible plan to complete dissertation within 2 years? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Writing Sample Writing Sample 2 Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11378": {"title": "Scheduling/Operations Specialist", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Scheduling/Operations Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Scheduling/Operations Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. The College requires that all applicants and employees be able to perform the essential functions of the job and will explore reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00897 Position Title Scheduling/Operations Specialist Division Student Success Division Department Name Office of the Registrar Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview Reporting to the Associate Registrar, the Scheduling/Operations Specialist supports the Registrar\u2019s Office with course registration, academic scheduling, and student records for undergraduate, graduate, and BPS programs. The position is responsible for maintaining accurate records and schedules across systems such as PeopleSoft and EMS , while assisting with enrollment, classroom assignments, and student record changes. The Specialist works closely with students, faculty, academic departments, and campus offices to resolve scheduling and data issues and ensure compliance with College policies. The role also supports reporting, data analysis, semester enrollment processes, and end-of-term system updates. Additionally, the Specialist provides guidance on academic policies, FERPA , and related procedures while delivering timely and professional customer service. Primary Purpose Reporting to the Associate Registrar, the Scheduling/Operations Specialist will assist with all aspects of the course registration and scheduling process. The Scheduling/Operations Specialist is pivotal in maintaining accurate and timely records for the College\u2019s undergraduate, graduate, and BPS programs, providing crucial administrative support for student data input and analysis, process review, and reporting. They will assist the Registrar\u2019s Office to ensure all functions are being performed accurately and in a timely manner: course registrations and withdrawals, Grade Changes, Changes in major/minor, FERPA consent forms, etc\u2026 The Scheduling/Operations Specialist is responsible for assisting students, faculty, and staff on college academic policies and procedures including FERPA . Essential Duties Support all facets of developing, managing, and communicating the college\u2019s master academic schedule, including coordinating with the calendar committee and other college departments. Identify scheduling discrepancies and work with Associate Registrar to provide solutions based on established guidelines and compliance to ensure the integrity and accuracy of the master schedules, particularly in developing multiple semester scheduling. Assist with the auditing of department course schedules to ensure college academic polices as outlined in MAPP are followed. Reconcile the college\u2019s student information system PeopleSoft, scheduling software, and the facilities database ( EMS ) to ensure general purpose classroom data is accurate and up-to-date across all systems. Collaborate with academic departments and campus administration to assign academic spaces for classes and events and devise creative solutions for complex issues related to the general-purpose classroom inventory. Input the course schedule room assignments into the EMS system by determined dates for each semester, and serve as a liaison with administrative offices that have shared responsibilities for centrally managed classrooms (Facilities Planning and Management, Information Technology Services, etc. Work with disability services and human resources to ensure ADA needs of students and faculty are met in classroom assignments. Assist with end of term programming and system rollover. Support the research, resolution, and reporting of enrollment and enrollment errors/data discrepancies between NSC , NSLDS , and the college\u2019s student information system in compliance with federal guidelines. Contribute to data collection and analysis to improve the college\u2019s curriculum and instruction management infrastructure to aid in planning, documentation, and reporting. Responsible for properly maintaining student and academic records in the College\u2019s SIS \u2013 PeopleSoft. Support the programming of PeopleSoft, each semester, with the approved enrollment appointment times for students. Assist with the enrollment verification process each semester, including running and distributing reports which identify students who have not attended all or some of their courses, and updating PeopleSoft accordingly. Support the credentialing functions of the Registrar\u2019s Office including student records, transcripts, and degree verification for all student types. Process student record changes, including but not limited to: change of program/major, incomplete grades, change of grade, course withdrawal, college withdrawal, and readmission to the college; as well as overall grading and transcript/record distinctions such as Dean\u2019s List. Provide effective and timely communication and customer service to all constituents by responding promptly and professionally to inquiries received via email, phone, or in person. Meets with individual students, faculty, staff, department chairs, and deans who have specific registrar related questions. Maintain confidentiality of student records and meetings with students in accordance with FERPA laws and regulations. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Registrar. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Thorough understanding of applicable academic policies and procedures relevant to Registrar\u2019s Office functions. Applies that knowledge to provide information, to problem solve, and to process information. Strong attention to detail. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to work effectively and collegially with students, faculty, and staff. Experience with contemporary computer technology. Ability to work independently. Demonstrated ability to represent the college positively and effectively with students, faculty, staff, higher education colleagues, and the public. Evidence of commitment to professional growth and development. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor\u2019s degree. Experience : Two years of experience with academic advising and/or student records in a higher education institution. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree. Experience in Higher Education Experience with student information systems such as PeopleSoft. Does this position have Direct Reports? No Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 10NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $60,000-$68,000 Work Schedule Monday-Friday 8:30am-4:30pm Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Associate Registrar Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Continuing End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit PSA Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 10/09/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. The College requires that all applicants and employees be able to perform the essential functions of the job and will explore reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned bachelor's degree? yes no * Do you have two years of experience with academic advising and/or student records in a higher education institution? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/10117": {"title": "Graduate Studies Instructor &amp; Writing Instructor", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Graduate Studies Instructor &amp; Writing Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Graduate Studies Instructor & Writing Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Detail Information Posting Number NT00116 Position Title/Assigment Graduate Studies Instructor & Writing Instructor Department Name Position Type Staff - Casual Position Description Posting Information Number of Positions Available Benefits Eligible? No Application Open Date 02/11/2026 Additional Information EEO Statement As an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity institution that values and is committed to inclusion and expanding the diversity of its faculty and staff, the College invites members of protected classes, including minorities and persons with disabilities, to identify themselves as such at the time of application. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master's degree or higher in English, Writing, Education, or a related field? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11350": {"title": "Associate Director Human Resources, Talent Management", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Associate Director Human Resources, Talent Management Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Associate Director Human Resources, Talent Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00884 Position Title Associate Director Human Resources, Talent Management Division President's Office Division Department Name Human Resources Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview Rhode Island College is seeking a strategic and highly collaborative HR professional to lead our team in the role of Associate Director of Human Resources, Talent Management. As the Associate Director you will have the opportunity to create and lead programs that make a meaningful difference in the employee experience. This is a highly visible role for an HR professional who enjoys building\u2014not simply maintaining\u2014talent programs and turning ideas into strategies, programs, and results. If you are energized by developing people, building programs and leading change this is an opportunity to contribute and make a positive impact on the employee eexperience. Primary Purpose The Associate Director Human Resources, Talent Management plays a central role in enhancing the college\u2019s capacity to adapt, evolve, and thrive in a dynamic educational landscape. The Associate Director is responsible for leading efforts to constantly improve recruiting efforts, implement professional development initiatives, talent development, data analysis, and process improvement. Providing strategic and operational leadership, the Associate Director will lead a team of professionals to deliver comprehensive initiatives. Essential Duties Strategic Initiatives & Implementation Define and advance the college\u2019s vision and long-term priorities for all staff and faculty learning, management and executive development, organizational effectiveness, and talent mobility impacting the entire college community. Serve as a principal advisor on college-wide strategies for staff development, engagement, retention, and organizational effectiveness. Build and sustain robust partnerships with HR leaders, academic, and administrative partners to develop and implement integrated, campus-wide talent strategies and ensure alignment with the college\u2019s mission and strategic goals. Lead, inspire, and develop a highly effective team. Ensure all programs are compliant with college collective bargaining agreements, state procedures, and federal/state laws. Remain competent and current through self-directed professional reading, developing professional contacts with colleagues, attending professional development courses, and attending training and/or courses as needed. Design and develop new HR processes to improve the efficiency of operations and recommend new approaches to effect continual improvement of processes and operations. Talent Acquisition Oversee full cycle recruiting efforts. Build and maintain recruiting strategies and best practices. Promote a positive image of the college as an employee of choice. Identify and propose recruiting strategies and changes, keeping in line with industry best practices, that align with business needs. Implement strategies to establish and iterate on pre\u2014boarding and onboarding processes. Talent Development Provide guidance to HR staff and department supervisors on the orientation and onboarding of new employees and troubleshoot as needed. Oversee communications with new employees during the on-boarding process. Responsible for monitoring the creation of new job descriptions and edits to existing job descriptions to align requirements across the college. Establish structure and evaluations for compensation philosophy, equity, and job families/structure across the college. Evaluate retention metrics across college and report on trends. Establish best practices for position management utilizing systems and processes. Professional Development & Employee Engagement Design and implement talent development programs to build leadership capabilities, enhance employee skills, and foster a culture of learning and growth. Provide strategic oversight for all training and development programs, ensuring accessibility and excellence for staff at every level and across all career stages. Lead the design, delivery, and continuous enhancement of college\u2019s comprehensive learning and development ecosystem, including in-person, blended, and digital modalities. Lead and support change management, employee engagement strategies (with a focus on retention and meaningful engagement), and organizational transformation initiatives through consultation and facilitation for leaders and their teams. Develop and implement strategies to enhance employee engagement, satisfaction, and retention. Data Analysis and Evaluation Track, measure, and communicate the impact and return on investment of talent programs, leveraging metrics such as satisfaction, usage, effectiveness, and organizational outcomes. Regularly conduct feedback for stakeholders including candidates on their experience. Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Occasional Duties Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Demonstrated proficiency utilizing HR information systems, applicant tracking systems, position management systems, databases, and Microsoft 365 applications. Demonstrated experience with HR agile values and agile principles. Knowledge of relevant human resources related laws, regulations, and best practices and the ability to apply them appropriately, including those related to HR processes. Knowledge of and ability to interpret and apply applicable State, Council, and College policies and procedures related to human resources, recruitment, selection, and employment. Ability to drive strategy, work with data and analytics, and a demonstrated capability in executing effective and creative strategies. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in Human Resource Management, Business Administration, Management, or a related field. A minimum of eight (8) years of experience in human resources, talent acquisition, talent management, recruitment and selection, onboarding, or a related area. Proven work experience in a Talent Acquisition//Talent Management role along with demonstrated experience in designing and implementing overall strategies for an organization. Supervisory, staff development or experience coordinating the work of employees. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Human Resources or similar field Experience working in a higher education and/or unionized environment. Experience working with Workday, PeopleAdmin, and/or comparable HRIS and applicant tracking systems. Bilingual in English / Spanish. Certifications: IPMA , CP or SCP certification through the Society for Human Resource Management ( SHRM ) or Professional in Human Resources ( PHR ) or Senior Professional in Human Resources ( SPHR ) or related certification. Does this position have Direct Reports? Yes Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 14NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $115,000 - $125,000 Work Schedule Monday \u2013 Friday, 8:30am \u2013 4:30pm 35 hours/week This position is located on-site. Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Director of Human Resources Operations Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Continuing End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit Non-union Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 09/15/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a earned Bachelor\u2019s degree in Human Resource Management, Business Administration, Management, or a related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of eight (8) years of experience in human resources, talent acquisition, talent management, recruitment and selection, onboarding, or a related area? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11328": {"title": "Adjunct, Marketing", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjunct, Marketing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjunct, Marketing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position. UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC/AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld. There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available . Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1,683/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjunct, Marketing Department Name Management and Marketing Department Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name School of Management Position Overview Adjunct Teaching Position in Marketing Department, courses taught would include Principles of Marketing and other marketing courses ( Advertising, Personal Selling & Sales Management, Global Marketing, Marketing Communications & Promotion, Digital Marketing) depending on candidate experience Essential Duties Course preparation Lecturing Grading Assist students Communication with students. Teach courses that meet once or twice a week and will be taught in person. Occasional Duties Email communications with department Chair and other faculty Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Familiarity with a learning management system. Knowledge of marketing principles and methods. Ability to engage students in active learning. Required Qualifications Minimum of a Master\u2019s degree in Marketing, Business Administration or related field as well as some post-secondary teaching experience with related industry experience. Preferred Qualifications A minimum of 2- year college teaching experience with industry experience in marketing. Environmental Conditions This is an in person class taught in a RIC classroom Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00053 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available 1 Anticipated Start Date or Semester Fall 2026 Posting Date 05/27/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position. UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC / AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld. There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available . Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have Master's degree in Marketing, Business Administration or related field as well as some post-secondary teaching experience with related industry experience? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11323": {"title": "Adjunct, Department of Educational Studies", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjunct, Department of Educational Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjunct, Department of Educational Studies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis as instructional and supervisory needs arise. The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development welcomes applications from individuals committed to excellence in teaching, mentoring, supervision, and professional preparation. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1,683/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjunct, Department of Educational Studies Department Name Educational Studies Department Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Feinstein School of Education and Human Development Position Overview The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development ( FSEHD ) at Rhode Island College prepares educators, counselors, school psychologists, wellness and exercise science, and youth development professionals who positively impact schools, communities, and the lives of children, youth, and adults. The FSEHD is committed to excellence, equity, inclusion, community engagement, and preparing highly qualified professionals throughout Rhode Island and beyond. The FSEHD invites applications from qualified professionals interested in serving as adjunct faculty teaching content, practicum, or seminar courses and/or supervising student teachers or interns across its undergraduate and graduate programs. Essential Duties Adjunct faculty may be assigned to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, supervise clinical experiences, or facilitate seminars. Department of Educational Studies \u2013 Programs: Secondary Education English, Mathematics, or History/Social Studies Foundations of Education: Introductory to Teaching ( FNED 101) and Learning Schooling for Social Justice ( FNED 246) World Language Education Assignments may include: Teaching undergraduate or graduate content courses. Teaching practicum, internship, or seminar courses. Serving as a college supervisor. Supervising student teachers or interns in PK-12 settings or counseling, youth development, or wellness and exercise community organizations. Contact : Charlie McLaughlin, Chair of the Department of Educational Studies Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Dean of the FSEHD . Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree. Relevant professional experience in the field. Appropriate licensure, certification, or credentials, where applicable. Experience working with diverse learners and communities. Strong communication, mentoring, and supervisory skills. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate Degree preferred. Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00068 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available Multiple Anticipated Start Date or Semester Posting Date 07/09/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis as instructional and supervisory needs arise. The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development welcomes applications from individuals committed to excellence in teaching, mentoring, supervision, and professional preparation. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11318": {"title": "Adjunct, Department of Computer Science and Information Systems", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjunct, Department of Computer Science and Information Systems Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjunct, Department of Computer Science and Information Systems Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1,683/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjunct, Department of Computer Science and Information Systems Department Name Computer Science and Information Systems Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name School of Management Position Overview The Department of Computer Science and Information Systems at Rhode Island College is seeking a dynamic and qualified educator for an adjunct faculty position in our department, with particular emphasis on cybersecurity, artificial intelligence, or general computer science. Essential Duties Teach a range of undergraduate courses in computer science, with possible specialization in cybersecurity, artificial intelligence, or related fields Deliver instruction across multiple modalities: in-person, hybrid, and online formats Develop and maintain course materials and assessments aligned with program learning outcomes Provide academic advising and mentorship to computer science students Participate in departmental meetings and contribute to curriculum development Maintain regular office hours for student support and consultation Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Dean, School of business. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree or higher in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Artificial Intelligence, or a closely related field. Demonstrated teaching experience or aptitude at the college/university level. Proficiency with online learning management systems and educational technologies. Strong communication skills and commitment to student success. Ability to effectively teach across different modalities (in-person, hybrid, and online). Preferred Qualifications Industry experience in cybersecurity, AI, software development, or related technical fields Experience teaching diverse student populations Evidence of innovative teaching approaches and student engagement strategies Knowledge of current trends and emerging technologies in computer science education Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00067 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available Multiple Anticipated Start Date or Semester Posting Date 07/09/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11395": {"title": "Associate Dean Feinstein School of Education and Human Development", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Associate Dean Feinstein School of Education and Human Development Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Associate Dean Feinstein School of Education and Human Development Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00872 Position Title Associate Dean Feinstein School of Education and Human Development Division Academic Affairs Division Department Name Feinstein School of Education and Human Development Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview The Associate Dean, reporting to and working closely with the Dean, will work to advance the FSEHD mission, vision, and core values with a focus on quality and status of the school\u2019s academic programs. In this capacity, the Associate Dean leads processes and procedures to support admissions, accreditation, and student success for educator preparation and community programs at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The Associate Dean provides leadership for program development, budgeting and innovative educator certification pathways. A key role is monitoring data trends in admission, progression, and completion to ensure robust enrollment and student-centered success. The Associate Dean also provides essential oversight in curriculum proposals, faculty load, and ensuring that course scheduling aligns with collective bargaining agreements and institutional policies. The Associate Dean works collaboratively with members of the Dean\u2019s Cabinet, including the Office of Partnerships and Placements, the Director of Assessment and Accreditation, and the Graduate Studies Director, to advance the FSEHD mission and strategic priorities. The Associate Dean also assists the Dean with operational and administrative matters and supports administrative staff on academic issues and represents the Dean in their absence. Primary Purpose The Associate Dean, reporting to and working closely with the Dean, will work to advance the FSEHD mission, vision, and core values with a focus on quality and status of the school\u2019s academic programs. In this capacity, the Associate Dean leads processes and procedures to support admissions, accreditation, and student success for educator preparation and community programs at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The Associate Dean provides leadership for program development, budgeting and innovative educator certification pathways. A key role is monitoring data trends in admission, progression, and completion to ensure robust enrollment and student-centered success. The Associate Dean also provides essential oversight in curriculum proposals, faculty load, and ensuring that course scheduling aligns with collective bargaining agreements and institutional policies. The Associate Dean works collaboratively with members of the Dean\u2019s Cabinet, including the Office of Partnerships and Placements, the Director of Assessment and Accreditation, and the Graduate Studies Director, to advance the FSEHD mission and strategic priorities. The Associate Dean also assists the Dean with operational and administrative matters and supports administrative staff on academic issues and represents the Dean in their absence. Essential Duties Admissions and Student Success \u25cf In collaboration with the FSEHD Dean\u2019s Office and faculty and staff, provide leadership and support for: \u25cb The planning, implementation, assessment, and continuous improvement of undergraduate and graduate academic programs, student success initiatives, and strategic priorities of the FSEHD . \u25cb Student recruitment, enrollment, retention, success, and engagement initiatives that advance the mission and strategic priorities of the FSEHD . Specific priorities include: \u25cb Coordinate progression into teacher candidacy for undergraduate teacher education students \u25cb Meet with students regarding academic standing, grievances, and appeals. \u25cb Coordinate with the Office of Partnerships and Placements on licensure test preparation efforts. Program and Curriculum Support \u25cf Ensure consistency in undergraduate and graduate policies, procedures, academic standards, and student support services across departments. \u25cf Oversee curriculum proposals through Undergraduate Curriculum Committee ( UCC ) and Graduate Curriculum Committee ( GCC ) processes. \u25cf Provide oversight and support for innovative pathways to education certification including the Credential Review Pathway, Registered Teaching Apprenticeship Program and other certification initiatives. \u25cf Work closely with the Dean and Chairs to accomplish expected program outcomes, advance innovative pedagogy and support student achievement and retention. Accreditation, and Continuous Quality Improvement \u25cf Coordinate unit-level accreditation reports and collaborate with OPP on annual Title II reporting. \u25cf Collaborate with the Director of Assessment on ongoing data collection efforts for teacher education programs. \u25cf Oversee the state approval process for new teacher education programs and coordinate academic planning, curriculum development, and program review for undergraduate and graduate programs. FSEHD Operations \u25cf Oversee full-time and adjunct faculty loads, course schedules and course enrollment patterns. \u25cf Monitor departmental adherence to collective bargaining agreements. \u25cf Coordinate updates to the website. \u25cf Collaborate closely with the Office of Partnerships and Placements ( OPP ), Director of Assessment, and Director of Graduate Programs to support teacher preparation and community-based program improvement. \u25cf Serve on the Dean\u2019s Leadership Committee and support operational effectiveness and communication systems to improve efficiencies. Partnerships and Engagement \u25cf Coordinate relationships between FSEHD and the Faculty of Arts and Sciences. \u25cf Serve as a liaison to college offices including Records, Office of Academic Support and Information Services, Communications and other offices across the College. \u25cf Coordinate articulation efforts with the University of Rhode Island, the Community College of Rhode Island, and the Council on Postsecondary Education. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Dean, FSEHD . Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Excellent oral and written communication, interpersonal and presentation skills. Evidence of scholarly accomplishment suitable for appointment at a senior faculty level. Demonstrated commitment to shared decision-making and collaboration. Ability to work effectively with various campus offices in supporting students. Ability to respond to emerging needs while effectively managing the day to day details of the position. Ability to work as impactful team member in providing leadership to a public institution of higher education. Required Qualifications Education: Earned doctoral degree from an accredited institution. Experience: Experience with accreditation and or program approval standards and processes. Qualifications consistent with appointment as a tenured associate or full professor. Preferred Qualifications Academic leadership experience in higher education. Successful teaching as a faculty member in a college or university school of education. Previous experience in PK-12 schools. Does this position have Direct Reports? No Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 18NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $130,000 - $150,000 Work Schedule Full-Time Monday-Friday 8:30AM-4:30PM Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Dean, FSEHD Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Continuing End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit Non-union Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 10/19/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a earned doctoral degree from an accredited institution? Yes No * Do you have experience with accreditation and or program approval standards and processes? Yes No * Do you have qualifications consistent with appointment as a tenured associate or full professor? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11204": {"title": "Teacher of the Visually Impaired", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Teacher of the Visually Impaired Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Teacher of the Visually Impaired Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00880 Position Title Teacher of the Visually Impaired Division Academic Affairs Division Department Name Sherlock Center, Vision Education and Services Program Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview The Sherlock Center invites applications for a Teacher of the Visually Impaired, Paul V. Sherlock Center on Disabilities. The individual will work as an itinerant vision educator conducting vision assessments, providing vision instruction and other duties assigned by the director. The Paul V. Sherlock Center on Disabilities, founded at Rhode Island College in 1993, is a University Center for Excellence in Developmental Disabilities ( UCEDD ). UCEDDs are evidence driven and designed to advance policies, practices and research that improve the health, education, social and economic well-being of people with disabilities, their families, and their communities. The mission of the Sherlock Center is to promote membership of individuals with disabilities in school, work and the community. Primary Purpose This teacher will be responsible for direct specialized instruction as well as indirect services to students who are blind or visually impaired (ages 3-21) as a member of a trans-disciplinary team in a variety of settings. Essential Duties Assessment and Evaluation: obtain and interpret for the TEAM , all eye related information, conduct and interpret functional vision and learning media assessments, recommend and collaborate in additional assessments as needed (low vision, physical therapy, occupational therapy, psychological, speech and language, etc). Participate in the development and implementation of Individualized Education Plans as a member of the trans-disciplinary TEAM . Provide direct, specialized instruction of developmental and compensatory skills as they relate to vision and visual impairment. These may include: Braille reading and writing (pre-Braille, Grade 1 and 2, Nemeth, etc.), concept development, visual efficiency, print adaptations and learning devices, handwriting, typewriting, listening skills, study skills, tactual skills, communication development, motor development, activities of daily living, physical education, leisure and recreation, career education, and transition skills. Provide training and consultation to teachers, therapists, and support staff on the impact of vision loss as well as educational accommodations, modifications, and strategies necessary for full access to the general core curriculum and the expanded core curriculum. Prepare, obtain, and disseminate specialized materials and books \u2013 with an emphasis on developing and communicating timelines with appropriate personnel to ensure that materials are available when needed. Be knowledgeable of state regulations and procedures for referrals, assessments, IEP development, and progress reports. Consult with students, parents, teachers, counselors, and other school personnel regarding private and public agencies, schools, and resources within the community for students who are blind or visually impaired. Participate in developing, coordinating, and/or providing the continuum of related services needed by students who are blind or visually impaired. Collaborate with school technology personnel as well as agencies and vendors to assist in the assessment and use of assistive technology. Maintain records of student assessments, IEPs, reviews, release forms, etc. following policies regarding confidentiality. Maintain records of material and equipment requests, census information, etc. Participate in professional development activities. Occasional Duties Other related work as assigned by the RIVESP Program Coordinator and/or the Director of the Paul V. Sherlock Center on Disabilities. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Comprehensive and up-to-date knowledge of best practices for children who are blind or visually impaired. Must be proficient in Grade II Braille and Nemeth Code. Ability to conduct functional vision and learning media assessments of children who are blind or visually impaired. Ability to develop, support, and monitor appropriate learning environments for students who are blind or visually impaired. This may include in-service training of school personnel, assisting with the training and monitoring of instructional assistants, and/or directly assisting the student in academic subjects and activities. Knowledge of core general curriculum and expanded core curriculum. Possession of technical skills in the use of assistive technology, computers, specialized devices, and effective instructional techniques. Strong organizational, communication, and report writing skills as necessary in an itinerant model. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Education of children who are blind or visually impaired. Certifications: Eligible for Rhode Island Teacher Certification as a Teacher of Children who are blind and visually impaired. Experience: Experience with children who are blind or visually impaired. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s Degree Does this position have Direct Reports? No Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to any adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade Not Applicable Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $59,238 - $108,049 (Salary calculated based on years of experience) Work Schedule Full-time, calendar year,182 school days to include summer school schedule Benefits Full-time employee benefits include: Comprehensive Health Benefits and Rewards for Wellness Incentives Generous Paid Time Off Family/Parental Leave Tuition Waivers at RIC , CCRI & URI Retirement Plan Long-term Disability Coverage Variety of voluntary add-on\u2019s For a complete listing, visit: http://www.employeebenefits.ri.gov/benefits/new/index.php Reports To (Title) Associate Director, Paul V. Sherlock Center on Disabilities Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Grant-funded End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit HUT Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 08/25/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree in education of children who are blind or visually impaired? Yes No * Do you have experience working with children who are blind or visually impaired? Yes No * Are you eligible for the Rhode Island Teacher Certification as a Teacher of Children who are blind and visually impaired? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11001": {"title": "Educational Advocate (Surrogate Parent)", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Educational Advocate (Surrogate Parent) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Educational Advocate (Surrogate Parent) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00837 Position Title Educational Advocate (Surrogate Parent) Division Academic Affairs Division Department Name Sherlock Center on Disabilities Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview Are you passionate about equity, education, and ensuring every child has a voice? Join Rhode Island College\u2019s Paul V. Sherlock Center on Disabilities as an Educational Advocate , where you\u2019ll play a critical role in championing the educational rights of children in DCYF care who have\u2014or may have\u2014disabilities. In this dynamic, student-centered role, you will serve as a trusted advocate and collaborator, working directly with schools, families, DCYF , CASA , and legal partners to ensure students receive the educational supports and services they are entitled to. You\u2019ll be deeply involved in the special education process\u2014from reviewing records and initiating evaluations to attending IEP and disciplinary meetings\u2014while monitoring school compliance and helping shape meaningful educational plans. This position is ideal for a proactive, detail-oriented professional who thrives in collaborative environments, understands education and child welfare systems, and is driven by the belief that every child deserves access to a high-quality, supportive education . Your work will have real, lasting impact\u2014not only on individual students, but across school systems statewide. If you\u2019re energized by advocacy, skilled in communication and collaboration, and committed to improving outcomes for children with disabilities, this role offers meaningful work with purpose and impact. Primary Purpose The individual will serve as an educational advocate for children who are in the care of DCYF and who have or are suspected of having a disability. Essential Duties Provide educational advocacy services to assigned students, including: Collecting and reviewing school records, including evaluations, discipline report, attendance records and other relevant information. Making referrals for special education evaluation when appropriate. -Visiting schools and observing classrooms for assigned students as appropriate. Participating in eligibility team meetings, disciplinary meetings, IEP meetings and other school meetings for assigned students. Maintaining familiarity with available resources for students with disabilities in the assigned districts. Working cooperatively with various service providers, including CASA and DCYF , regarding educational planning for students. Monitoring the performance of local school departments in complying with the IEPs of assigned students Keep accurate and up-to-date records, file reports and assist in the preparation of cases with staff attorneys and supervisors. -Provide resources and information to Rhode Island College faculty and students. -Attend IEP meetings and other school meetings as necessary. Attend staff meetings and training sessions as scheduled. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Director, Paul V. Sherlock Center on Disabilities Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Knowledge of the General and Special Education systems. Knowledge of pertinent laws and regulations. Knowledge of the child welfare systems. Ability to collaborate with professionals, families and students. Effective communication skills (verbal, written and electronic). Ability to travel and arrange transportation to various public and private school locations throughout Rhode Island. Required Qualifications Education: College degree in a discipline related to the education of children or child welfare. Experience: Three years of experience with children with disabilities or children in child welfare. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in special education or child welfare systems in Rhode Island. Bilingual. Does this position have Direct Reports? No Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Off campus facilities may not be accessible to persons who are disabled. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 9NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range 51,401 Work Schedule Monday \u2013 Friday 8:30- 4:30 Some evenings and weekends Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Coordinator, Educational Advocate Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Grant-funded End of Temporary or Limited Position 06/19/2027 Collective Bargaining Unit Non-union Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 03/31/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a college degree in discipline related to the education of children or child welfare? Yes No * Do you have three years of experience with children with disabilities or children in child welfare? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11380": {"title": "Housekeeper", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Housekeeper Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Housekeeper Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. At the time of appointment, the applicant must be physically qualified to perform assigned duties as evidenced by a physician\u2019s certificate. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Information Position Information Posting Number CS00648 Position Title Housekeeper Division Administration and Finance Division Department Name Custodial Services Position Type Staff \u2013 Classified General Statement of Duties To do cleaning, custodial and simple maintenance work at a university or college; to follow daily custodial standards and instructions; and to do related work as required. Supervision Received Duties are assigned individually, usually in detail; work is supervised while in process and reviewed upon completion for overall efficiency and effectiveness. Supervision Exercised Usually none. Position Overview The Housekeeper is responsible for maintaining clean, safe, and orderly university facilities. This position performs a variety of custodial and basic maintenance duties, including cleaning floors, carpets, restrooms, offices, classrooms, residence halls, athletic facilities, kitchens, and other campus spaces. Responsibilities also include collecting and disposing of waste and recyclables, restocking supplies, setting up rooms and equipment for events, cleaning windows and fixtures, operating custodial equipment, and reporting safety concerns or maintenance needs. The Housekeeper may also assist with snow removal, grounds maintenance, moving furniture, and other facility-related tasks as assigned. Illustrative Examples of Work Performed To clean (sweep, strip, dust, scrub, mop, wash or vacuum), polish or wax floors, carpets, walls, windows, woodwork, furniture and equipment in all university or college buildings, including offices, dining rooms, kitchens, bathrooms, rest rooms, showers, residence halls, athletic facilities, guest rooms, public spaces, conference rooms, laboratories and classrooms, corridors, entrances, exterior walkways, and building fixtures. To clean plumbing fixtures. To collect and dispose of trash, recyclables and other wastes. On occasion, to move, or assist in moving, office furniture and equipment. As directed, to spray and fumigate for insects, such as bees, ants, etc. To provide washrooms with soap, paper products and other necessary supplies. To observe and report unusual situations on property and grounds. To clean sidewalks and perform manual labor in connection with lawn and garden maintenance; to remove snow. To operate buffers, wet/dry vacuums and floor scrubbing machines, carpet extractors and pressure washers (with proper orientation). To wash and hang drapes, venetian and vertical blinds; to wash, dry and fold towels. To collect, separate and dispose of recyclable materials. To participate in setting up equipment in all university or college facilities; to set up conference rooms in the configuration requested by groups. To report on safety issues and the need for maintenance repairs. To change incandescent and florescent lights. To wash interior and exterior windows. Under direction, may be assigned to access computerized inventory systems; to stock supply closets based on need. To clean and wash all industrial rubber matting. To receive and stock supplies in appropriate areas. To clean and maintain tools and equipment after use. To do related work as required. Education Such as may have been gained through: completion of eight school grades. Experience Such as may have been gained through: functioning in a capacity requiring the performance of basic cleaning and custodial tasks. Or Combination of Education and Experience Any combination of education and experience that shall be substantially equivalent to the above education and experience. Additional Required Qualifications Knowledges Skills and Capacities A working knowledge of the equipment, materials and methods used in cleaning and custodial work; the ability to understand and carry out simple directions; and related capacities and abilities. Preferred Qualifications \u2022 Ability to carry 50 lbs. \u2022 Ability to stand, bend, reach, climb stairs, use ladder to perform tasks for seven productive hours daily. \u2022 Ability to work independently or as a team. \u2022 Ability to understand, communicate and receive verbal or written instruction in English. \u2022 Commercial cleaning experience. \u2022 Familiarity and experience operating but not limited to: ride on auto scrubbers, ride on burnishers, walk behind auto scrubbers, walk behind burnishers, window cleaning equipment (squeegee, power washer, extension pole cleaners), side by side floor scrubbers, hand operated burnisher, and mechanized carpet cleaning equipment. \u2022 Experience with APPA\u2019S levels of clean. \u2022 Knowledge of and experience practicing ISSA custodial standards. Position Details FLSA Non-Exempt Full Time / Part Time Full-time Work Schedule Full-Time, 40 hours per week Monday \u2013 Friday 6:00AM \u2013 2:30PM Floater Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Associate Director of Facilities & Operations, Custodial Services Position Status Permanent - C End of Restricted or Limited Position Civil Service List No Union Code classified Salary Grade 310CA Minimum Salary for Grade $44,366 Maximum Salary for Grade $47,454 Added Salary for This Position Collective Bargaining Unit Council 94 Local 2878 Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Anticipated Start Date 10/10/2026 Application Open Date Application Close Date 10/21/2026 Special Instructions At the time of appointment, the applicant must be physically qualified to perform assigned duties as evidenced by a physician\u2019s certificate. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/10365": {"title": "Science Instructor", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Science Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Science Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Positions are contingent upon the level of federal funding and student enrollment. Salary range: $2,800 to $3,500. The salary may be adjusted based on student enrollment. Candidates are required to upload a resume and cover letter. In the cover letter, please indicate the high school level course(s) the candidate is applying to teach: Biology, Chemistry, Environmental Science, Forensic Science, Human Anatomy/Physiology, Physics, and Advanced Physics, Robotics, AI, Computer Science, or VR. Provide the names and contact information for three current professional references. At least one reference must come from an educational administrator who has supervised the applicant. Please include the title of each person providing a reference. Taxes will be withheld from the salary, and payment will be made on August 7th. No fringe benefits will be provided. Attention foreign citizens working in the U.S. under a visa: This position is short-term, and Rhode Island College will not sponsor a work authorization visa. Before finalizing employment, this position requires successful completion of a background check, which may include, but is not limited to, verification of education, employment history, and a criminal and sex offender record check. The employee must also submit specific forms required by the RI College Human Resources Office as outlined in the terms. Posting Details Posting Detail Information Posting Number NT00126 Position Title/Assigment Science Instructor Department Name Position Type Staff - Casual Position Description Posting Information Number of Positions Available Benefits Eligible? No Application Open Date 02/18/2026 Additional Information Positions are contingent upon the level of federal funding and student enrollment. Salary range: $2,800 to $3,500. The salary may be adjusted based on student enrollment. Candidates are required to upload a resume and cover letter. In the cover letter, please indicate the high school level course(s) the candidate is applying to teach: Biology, Chemistry, Environmental Science, Forensic Science, Human Anatomy/Physiology, Physics, and Advanced Physics, Robotics, AI, Computer Science, or VR. Provide the names and contact information for three current professional references. At least one reference must come from an educational administrator who has supervised the applicant. Please include the title of each person providing a reference. Taxes will be withheld from the salary, and payment will be made on August 7th. No fringe benefits will be provided. Attention foreign citizens working in the U.S. under a visa: This position is short-term, and Rhode Island College will not sponsor a work authorization visa. Before finalizing employment, this position requires successful completion of a background check, which may include, but is not limited to, verification of education, employment history, and a criminal and sex offender record check. The employee must also submit specific forms required by the RI College Human Resources Office as outlined in the terms. EEO Statement As an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity institution that values and is committed to inclusion and expanding the diversity of its faculty and staff, the College invites members of protected classes, including minorities and persons with disabilities, to identify themselves as such at the time of application. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * 1. * Are you available to meet the required time commitments set forth in this summer job description? yes no * Have you taught this subject for at least 2 years to groups of low-income, first-generation high school students in a formal classroom setting, with at least fifteen students in each group? Yes No * Have you at least 2 years of experience developing course curriculum and learning objectives aligned to Common Core/State Standards? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document (see special instructions) Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11359": {"title": "Athletic Facility and Events Management and Operations Assistant", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Athletic Facility and Events Management and Operations Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Athletic Facility and Events Management and Operations Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00882 Position Title Athletic Facility and Events Management and Operations Assistant Division President's Office Division Department Name Athletics and Recreation Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview The Athletic Facility and Events Management and Operations Assistant is a full-time, calendar-year position at Rhode Island College that supports the management, maintenance, and daily operations of athletic and recreation facilities. Reporting to the Assistant Director of Athletic and Recreation Facilities, the Assistant helps ensure facilities are safe, well-maintained, and prepared for intercollegiate athletics, campus programs, and community events. The Assistant coordinates event preparation and operations, including scheduling, setup, staffing, ticket sales, and teardown. Responsibilities also include supporting the care of outdoor athletic fields and courts, maintaining facility equipment, conducting safety inspections, and coordinating work orders with the College\u2019s Physical Plant and outside vendors. The role communicates facility rules and operating hours and assists with departmental fundraising activities and camps. Primary Purpose This position will assist and support the overall management and operations of athletic and recreation facilities, including scheduling, setup, teardown, security, and maintenance. Essential Duties Coordinate and assist in the management of playing fields and facilities to accommodate both intercollegiate, institutional and community activities including set-up, staffing, etc. Support all intercollegiate contest management functions (i.e., set-up, tear down, ticket sales, etc.). Coordinate all work orders with the College\u2019s Physical Plant and outside vendors to ensure that work is completed in an expeditious manner. Implement a plan to insure the maintenance and safety of all Departmental facilities (to include ongoing inspections). Responsible for the maintenance and upkeep of athletic/recreational facility equipment (i.e., scoreboards, goal posts, bleachers, fencing, mowing equipment, tractors, etc.). Ensure that facility rules, regulations, and hours of operation are properly communicated. Directly responsible to support the care, upkeep and maintenance of the College\u2019s tennis, baseball, softball, soccer, and outdoor track facilities. Responsible for oversight of facilities as it relates to intercollegiate, recreation and community based contracted events (i.e., practices, contests, RIIL events, Open House, etc.). Perform related duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Assistant Director. Assist in departmental fundraising activities including camps. Occasional Duties Perform other related duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Assistant Director and Director. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Good interpersonal skills and the ability to interact with a diverse group of constituents. Knowledge about the specific maintenance requirements of athletic facilities and fields gained by attendance at appropriate seminars. Excellent communication skills (both written and oral). Knowledge of the NCAA and its rules, regulations and philosophies; with specific knowledge as it relates to facilities. Valid Driver\u2019s License. Valid Certification in First Aid and CPR or agreement to obtain. Valid RI State Fire Marshall Event Oversight certification or agreement to obtain. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor\u2019s Degree in related field. Experience: A minimum of three years of progressive experience in the management and maintenance of athletic/recreational facilities at the intercollegiate level. Preferred Qualifications Bilingual. Does this position have Direct Reports? No Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 10NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $60,000 - $65,000 Work Schedule Non-Standard work week. Includes nights and weekends. Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Assistant Athletic Director for Athletics and Recreational Facilities Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Continuing End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit PSA Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 09/10/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor\u2019s Degree in related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of three years of progressive experience in the management and maintenance of athletic/recreational facilities at the intercollegiate level? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11330": {"title": "Adjunct, Health Education (Fall 2026)", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjunct, Health Education (Fall 2026) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjunct, Health Education (Fall 2026) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC/AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld. There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available . Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1,683/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjunct, Health Education (Fall 2026) Department Name Health and Physical Education Department Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Feinstein School of Education and Human Development Position Overview The Department of Health and Physical Education is seeking candidates to fill part-time instructor positions in teacher preparation health education courses, in particular practicum courses which require both coursework on campus, as well as partnering with RI schools. Supervision in the field is also required. Essential Duties Teach courses as needed at the undergraduate level. Occasional Duties Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Qualifications Education: Masters or Doctoral Degree in Health Education or Education Experience: 3 or more years K-12 teaching experience Knowledge of RI schools Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience at the college level. Environmental Conditions Teaching/instruction is performed in a traditional classroom setting. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00051 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available Multiple Anticipated Start Date or Semester Fal 2026 Semester Posting Date 04/21/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC / AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld. There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available . Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11325": {"title": "Adjunct, Graphic Design Instructor", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjunct, Graphic Design Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjunct, Graphic Design Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. -UNION ELIGIBILITY: Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC/AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. -Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. -Candidates are required to provide digital images of personal and student work, submitted as either a .pdf file or a link. Use the Multi Media 1 button (no cds, usb drives, or hard copies.) -Candidates are required to provide a teaching statement. Use the Teaching Philosophy 1 button. -During the application process candidates will be prompted to provide names and contact information for three current references. -An optional button has been provided in case candidates wish to upload additional information. Note: Candidates having specific questions can address their inquiries to: Professor Heemong Kim, (401-456-9691 or hkim@ric.edu) Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1,683/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjunct, Graphic Design Instructor Department Name Art Department Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Other Position Overview This position involves teaching undergraduate BA and BFA students the core concepts and practical skills of professional Graphic Design, guiding them from introductory foundations through advanced applications. The instructor will develop and deliver coursework that builds students\u2019 creative, conceptual, and technical abilities across key areas of the field, including typography, publication design, branding design, and package design. Essential Duties The individual will teach BA and BFA students professional Graphic Design concepts and skills from the beginning to advanced levels, such as typography, publication design, branding design, and package design. Occasional Duties Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Qualifications MFA in Graphic Design or comparable and significant professional experience or four-year degree and extensive professional experience. Preferred Qualifications College teaching experience. Environmental Conditions Graphic Design studio courses are taught in a Macintosh computer lab and are capped at 15 students. An adjacent seminar is available on select days/times. This facility includes a projector with a sound system, worktables, inkjet and color laser printers, paper cutters, a light box, book binding tools, a selection of other small tools for building projects, flat files, a ventilated spray room, a large storage closet, and cupboards. Floor-to-ceiling windows are equipped with blackout blinds. All graphic design students have access to open lab hours on select days. There is a shared adjunct office on the first floor of the Art Center. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00059 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available 1 Anticipated Start Date or Semester Posting Date 03/10/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions/Information for Applicants - UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC / AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. -Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. -Candidates are required to provide digital images of personal and student work, submitted as either a .pdf file or a link. Use the Multi Media 1 button (no cds, usb drives, or hard copies.) -Candidates are required to provide a teaching statement. Use the Teaching Philosophy 1 button. -During the application process candidates will be prompted to provide names and contact information for three current references. -An optional button has been provided in case candidates wish to upload additional information. Note: Candidates having specific questions can address their inquiries to: Professor Heemong Kim, (401-456-9691 or hkim@ric.edu) Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Multi Media Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11320": {"title": "Adjunct, Department of Counseling, Educational Leadership, and School Psychology", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjunct, Department of Counseling, Educational Leadership, and School Psychology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjunct, Department of Counseling, Educational Leadership, and School Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis as instructional and supervisory needs arise. The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development welcomes applications from individuals committed to excellence in teaching, mentoring, supervision, and professional preparation. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1,683/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjunct, Department of Counseling, Educational Leadership, and School Psychology Department Name Counseling, Educational Leadership, and School Psychology Department Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Feinstein School of Education and Human Development Position Overview The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development ( FSEHD ) at Rhode Island College prepares educators, counselors, school psychologists, wellness and exercise science, and youth development professionals who positively impact schools, communities, and the lives of children, youth, and adults. The FSEHD is committed to excellence, equity, inclusion, community engagement, and preparing highly qualified professionals throughout Rhode Island and beyond. The FSEHD invites applications from qualified professionals interested in serving as adjunct faculty teaching content, practicum, or seminar courses and/or supervising student teachers or interns across its undergraduate and graduate programs. Essential Duties Department of Counseling, Educational Leadership, and School Psychology ( CEP ) \u2013 Programs: Clinical Mental Health Counseling School Psychology Assignments may include: Teaching undergraduate or graduate content courses. Teaching practicum, internship, or seminar courses. Serving as a college supervisor. Supervising student teachers or interns in PK-12 settings or counseling, youth development, or wellness and exercise community organizations. Contact: Shannon Dowd-Eagle or Kalina Brabeck, Co-Chairs Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Dean of the FSEHD . Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree. Relevant professional experience in the field. Experience working with diverse learners and communities. Strong communication, mentoring, and supervisory skills. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate Degree preferred. Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00064 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available Multiple Anticipated Start Date or Semester Posting Date 07/01/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis as instructional and supervisory needs arise. The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development welcomes applications from individuals committed to excellence in teaching, mentoring, supervision, and professional preparation. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11256": {"title": "Wellness Coordinator", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Wellness Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Wellness Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Posting Detail Information Posting Number NT00134 Position Title/Assigment Wellness Coordinator Department Name Counselling Services Position Type Staff - Casual Position Description Primary Purpose The Wellness Coordinator plays a critical role in advancing the mission of the Center for Health & Wellness, including Health Services, the Counseling Center, and Learning for Life, by leading campus-wide prevention, education, and outreach initiatives. This position develops, implements, and evaluates programs that promote emotional well-being, reduce distress, and support students\u2019 holistic health and wellness. The Coordinator oversees campus-wide initiatives; tracks and responds to outreach requests from campus departments and local community partners; and builds collaborative relationships with campus stakeholders, student organizations, and community organizations to deliver high-impact educational programs, awareness campaigns, and outreach efforts. Through this work, the Wellness Coordinator supports the Center for Health & Wellness\u2019s mission to provide confidential, comprehensive, and holistic care to all RIC students and the broader campus community. Essential Job Functions Develops, implements and oversees programming initiatives to enhance the Center for Health & Wellness mission to reduce distress, promote emotional wellness, enhance life satisfaction, and improve overall well-being. Collaborate with Directors under the Center for Health and Wellness including the Director of Counseling, Director of Student Health Services and the Director for Learning 4 Life related to programming and educational initiatives. Build and maintain relationships with campus departments, student organizations, and local community partners to enhance programming efforts. Create, design, and implement wellness programming, including but not limited to group programs, presentations, and single-session workshops on topics relevant to current student concerns. Areas of focus to include but are not limited to, suicide prevention, substance use support services, and other mental health and wellness initiatives. Maintain timely and appropriate records for event attendance and content. Participate in the Counseling Center\u2019s liaison system with residence life staff; participate in training and consultation with faculty and professional and student staff to develop their skills in recognizing, responding to, and referring students in psychological distress. Serve as a liaison between the Center for Health and Wellness and campus departments, providing training and consultation to faculty, professional staff, and student staff. Support the development of their skills in identifying, responding to, and referring students experiencing psychological distress. Maintain accurate records of event attendance, programming content, and outreach requests. Work under the supervision of the Director of Counseling and/or designated senior staff. Occasional Job Functions Represent the Center for Health & Wellness at events, including some evening and weekend hours. Assist with administrative functions as needed. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of the Counseling Center. Required Qualifications Education: A Bachelor\u2019s degree in, psychology, social work, public health or related field. Experience: Experience working in a college/university counseling service or comparable outpatient facility. Strong public speaking and networking skills. Excellent written communication skills. Knowledge of community agencies and resources in the community. Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Benefits Eligible? No Application Open Date 08/26/2026 Additional Information Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree in, psychology, social work, public health or related field? yes no Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11385": {"title": "Campus Police Officer (RIC)", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Campus Police Officer (RIC) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Campus Police Officer (RIC) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Position Information Posting Number CS00646 Position Title Campus Police Officer (RIC) Division Administration and Finance Division Department Name Security and Safety Department Position Type Staff \u2013 Classified General Statement of Duties At Rhode Island College ( RIC ), to independently perform a full range of tasks involved in the protection, safety and security of individuals and property at Rhode Island College ( RIC ); to patrol the campus on foot, bicycle and/or in marked police cruisers; to inspect campus buildings and grounds; to guard against fire, theft, damage, defacement and/or destruction; to maintain order and security on institution premises; to identify and apprehend criminal offenders as permitted within the law and participate in subsequent Court proceedings; to provide emergency medical services to the campus community, including to provide aid to individuals who are injured or in danger of physical harm as well as to render first aid; to perform all required duties in accordance with applicable State and Federal laws and ordinances as well as College and Department rules, regulations, policies and orders; and to do related work as required. Supervision Received Works under the general and specific instructions of a RIC Campus Police Sergeant with occasional supervision from a RIC Campus Police Lieutenant; work is reviewed in process and upon completion for conformance to provisions of State and Federal laws and ordinances as well as College and Department rules, regulations, policies and orders to include annual performance evaluations. Supervision Exercised Usually none unless directed by a superior officer. Position Overview The purpose of the Campus Police Department is to provide service and protection to The Rhode Island College campus, properties, staff, faculty, visitors, and students. Working with Student Services, Residential Life, Physical Plant and others in our on-campus community, we are an integrated team striving to achieve excellence in police protection and to ensure a high quality of student-faculty life by promoting a tranquil, safe atmosphere conducive to the objectives of the College. The department is dedicated to the protection of the College properties to ensure the beauty, security, and safe function of the campus grounds and resources. Illustrative Examples of Work Performed At Rhode Island College ( RIC ), to independently perform a full range of tasks involved in the protection, safety and security of individuals and property at Rhode Island College ( RIC ); to patrol the campus on foot, bicycle and/or in marked police cruisers; to inspect campus buildings and grounds; to guard against fire, theft, damage, defacement and/or destruction; to maintain order and security on institution premises; to identify and apprehend criminal offenders as permitted within the law and participate in subsequent Court proceedings; to provide emergency medical services to the campus community, including to provide aid to individuals who are injured or in danger of physical harm as well as to render first aid; to perform all required duties in accordance with applicable State and Federal laws and ordinances as well as College and Department rules, regulations, policies and orders; and to do related work as required. To ensure all buildings are secure by locking and unlocking as needed. To attend roll call prior to the beginning of a shift. To acquire and record information concerning events that have occurred since the last shift. To reduce opportunities for the commission of crime through preventative law enforcement measures. To facilitate the movement of vehicular and pedestrian traffic through the enforcement of the Motor Vehicle Code. To proactively identify potential law enforcement problems and communicate the need for services by utilizing the Department Chain of Command. To actively participate in establishing and maintaining security and safety on the College campus. To promote and preserve peace on campus in a variety of settings including but not limited to campus gatherings, events, debates and/or during response to disturbances. To exercise authority consistent with the obligations imposed by the oath of office. To be accountable to supervisory Officers and promptly obey all lawful orders. To coordinate efforts with other members of the Department so that teamwork may ensure a continuity of purpose and the achievement of Department objectives. To communicate all pertinent information promptly and accurately to supervisors and fellow Officers. To acquire and record necessary information, and to document the provision of police services to any member of the campus community. To file all reports and documents prior to the end of each shift with care to ensure accuracy and completeness. To ensure that all property seized, recovered or taken for safekeeping is properly marked, receipted and stored prior to the completion of each shift. To maintain equipment properly and regularly in order to keep such equipment in a functional and presentable condition. To care for all assigned Department equipment in such manner as to prevent unnecessary damage. To carry out all duties in an efficient and professional manner which brings credit to the Officer, the College, the Department and the law enforcement profession. To assist and provide information to members of the campus community upon request. To courteously explain any instance where the Department does not have jurisdiction, and to make suggestions as to other procedures that the member of the campus community can follow to rectify the problem(s). To serve and/or deliver warrants, summonses, subpoenas and other official papers promptly in the manner prescribed by law and/or by the issuing supervisor and in keeping with campus policy. To confer with and generally assist Court prosecutors in furtherance of criminal prosecutions as needed. To appear in Court as summoned and to testify in a professional manner. To consistently refrain from the use of excessive force and the appearance of bias or prejudice when dealing with the public or those detained. To enforce all laws and ordinances in a fair and professional manner. To punctually respond to all assignments. To operate a communications office including dispatching and keeping police records. To perform routine maintenance on police vehicles. To cooperate with other law enforcement agencies in the enforcement of laws and regulations. To perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Director of Security and Safety, Chief of Campus Police or his/her designee. Education Possession of a high school diploma or GED plus successful completion of a Rhode Island Police Officer Standards and Training ( POST ) certified Police Training Academy curriculum. Experience Prior employment in a full-time position as a POST certified police officer, who retired or resigned in good standing, requiring maintenance of law and order and protection of life and property, including responsibility for the arrest and detention of persons in violation of the law. Or Combination of Education and Experience NA Additional Required Qualifications 1. Must possess valid Police Officer Standards and Training ( POST ) Certification 2. Must be physically qualified to perform assigned duties as evidenced by a physician\u2019s certificate 3. Must possess and maintain a valid motor vehicle operator\u2019s license 4. Ability to pass a national background criminal investigation ( BCI ) 5. Ability to pass a state-approved psychological examination. 6. Must pass a pre-employment drug screening and any random post-employment screening 7. Within 6 months of appointment, must acquire and maintain First Responder Certification from the Rhode Island Department of Health Knowledges Skills and Capacities A working knowledge of the Office of Postsecondary Commissioner\u2019s and assigned institutional regulations; a working knowledge of the principles and practices commonly applied by a police officer in the enforcement of the law and regulations to protect life and property; the ability to apply such knowledge, principles and practices in a college environment; a working knowledge of the methods of investigating accidents and other incidents; the ability to enforce traffic regulations and to direct and regulate traffic; the ability to make accurate reports on law or regulation violations; the ability to render first aid; the ability to operate a communications office and keep police records; the ability to cope with situations firmly, courteously, tactfully and with respect for the rights of others; the ability to analyze and appropriately act in emergency situations, develop effective courses of action and successfully facilitate safe outcomes to the same; the ability to understand and carry out oral and written instructions; the ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing; and related capacities and abilities. Preferred Qualifications NA Position Details FLSA Non-Exempt Full Time / Part Time Full-time Work Schedule 40 hours/week 3rd shift, 11:00PM \u2013 7:00AM Days off: Monday/Tuesday Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Director of Security & Safety / Chief of Campus Police Position Status Permanent - C End of Restricted or Limited Position Civil Service List No Union Code classified Salary Grade 323CA Minimum Salary for Grade $59,609 Maximum Salary for Grade $68,162 Added Salary for This Position $2/hr shift differential Collective Bargaining Unit Council 94 Local 2878 Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Anticipated Start Date 09/23/2026 Application Open Date Application Close Date Special Instructions EEO Statement As an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity institution that values and is committed to inclusion and expanding the diversity of its faculty and staff, the College invites members of protected classes, including minorities and persons with disabilities, to identify themselves as such at the time of application. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have prior employment in a full-time position as a POST certified police officer, who retired or resigned in good standing? Yes No * Did you successfully complete and graduate from the Rhode Island Municipal Police Training Academy, Rhode Island State Police Training Academy, or the Providence Police Training Academy? Yes No * Do you possess a valid Rhode Island Police Officer Standards and Training (POST) Certification? Yes No * Have you had any break in law enforcement service that exceeds five (5) years? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume R I M P A or Equivalent Certificate Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11054": {"title": "Cyber-Range Operator", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Cyber-Range Operator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Cyber-Range Operator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Compensation: $45 - $60 per hour Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Posting Detail Information Posting Number NT00132 Position Title/Assigment Cyber-Range Operator Department Name Institute for Cybersecurity & Emerging Technologies Position Type Staff - Casual Position Description Primary Purpose The Cyber Range Operator supports cyber resilience for students and community partners by organizing and executing high-intensity simulated cyberattack exercises in a state-of-the-art environment. These trainings are designed to evaluate participant preparedness, response effectiveness, and operational decision-making under pressures associated with data breaches and related cyber incidents. This role focuses on structured adversarial testing, incident escalation modeling, playbook readiness, and pre-and post-exercise analysis to educated students in the intricacies of cyber-defense and improve overall enterprise security posture. Essential job functions: Learn and facilitate cyberattack simulations within a controlled physical and logical environment. Support red-team and cyber range operations to evaluate defensive capabilities. Assist instructors in the delivery of educational cyberattack scenarios to students of all skill levels. Monitor and evaluate participant performance and response effectiveness during simulated incidents. Identify gaps in technical controls, communication workflows, and escalation procedures. Document findings and provide clear, actionable recommendations to stakeholders. Contribute to the development and refinement of incident response playbooks. Ensure all activities comply with organizational policies, legal requirements, and ethical standards. Ensure cyber range software/hardware and other administrative tasks are maintained and up-to-date as needed. Work with other Institute staff to ensure Range calendar and scheduling is kept current. Occasional job functions: Attend occasional meetings, events, and conferences related to cyber-range and/or Institute for Cybersecurity & Emerging Technologies. Travel to customer sites for range-related activities. Perform other duties as assigned by the Institute director. Required qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Information Security, Computer Science, or a related field and equivalent experience/certifications Professional experience in cybersecurity operations, incident response, or threat simulation. Expert knowledge of network security, system behavior, and attack/defense methodologies. Experience in a training or instruction environment. Ability to perform effectively in time-sensitive, high-pressure scenarios. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Preferred qualifications: Industry certifications such as CISSP , CEH , OSCP , or equivalent. Experience with cyber range platforms, tabletop exercises, or red-team engagements. Familiarity with regulatory and compliance frameworks (e.g., NIST , ISO , SOC 2). Experience working in enterprise or regulated environments. Environmental conditions: The employee is not exposed to any known adverse environmental conditions. Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Benefits Eligible? No Application Open Date 07/06/2026 Additional Information Compensation: $45 \u2013 $60 per hour Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have a Bachelor\u2019s degree in Information Security, Computer Science, or a related field and equivalent experience/certifications? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/10444": {"title": "Program Coordinator - Real Skills for Youth", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Program Coordinator - Real Skills for Youth Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Program Coordinator - Real Skills for Youth Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Period of employment: Until 12/31/2026 Compensation: $25-$30 per hour. Weekly hours: 10-15. Posting Details Posting Detail Information Posting Number NT00129 Position Title/Assigment Program Coordinator - Real Skills for Youth Department Name Position Type Staff - Casual Position Description Posting Information Number of Positions Available Benefits Eligible? No Application Open Date 03/13/2026 Additional Information Period of employment: Until 12/31/2026 Compensation: $25-$30 per hour. Weekly hours: 10-15. EEO Statement As an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity institution which values and is committed to expanding the diversity of its faculty and staff, the College invites members of protected classes, including minorities and persons with disabilities, to identify themselves as such at the time of application. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and experience? Yes No * Do you have between 1 and 3 years of experience in program coordination, administration, or a related role? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11371": {"title": "Assistant to the Director of Athletics", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Assistant to the Director of Athletics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Assistant to the Director of Athletics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00892 Position Title Assistant to the Director of Athletics Division President's Office Division Department Name Athletics and Recreation Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview The Assistant to the Director of Intercollegiate Athletics and Recreation helps shape a positive, engaging experience for student-athletes and the broader campus community. Working closely with the director, this role supports student-athlete success and keeps athletics and recreation programs running smoothly by coordinating student support services, team travel, facilities, and athletic events. The position also contributes to fundraising, community outreach, and marketing, while guiding student-athlete leadership activities and helping build school spirit and fan engagement. Primary Purpose To support the Director of Intercollegiate Athletics and Recreation in the planning, development, implementation, coordination and supervision of programs, and activities that are athletic and recreational in nature with special emphasis on student and student-athlete programming. Essential Duties Assist in the supervision and programming of the Department\u2019s student-athlete support services with ongoing emphasis on student-athlete success and retention (i.e., academic support and counseling, registration, prepare statistical reports, monitor enrollment, etc.). Assist in the overall and safe management of the Recreation Center with specific emphasis on the membership operation including the computation of relevant data (i.e., program attendance, etc.) and the support of ongoing fiscal controls. Assist in the overall and safe management of the Department\u2019s motor pool and transportation operation. Assist and support special community, and campus-based programming (i.e., CHOICES , community service projects, marketing events, summer camps, etc). Assist in departmental fundraising activities with special emphasis in the upgrading and upkeep delivery of an email, web-based, delivery system. Assist in the delivery of services (i.e., prepare purchasing reports, etc.), as well as the maintenance of inventory of the Department\u2019s equipment operation. Assist in contest management to insure a safe, friendly, and professional environment for users and patrons, manage and program in-house ticket production system (i.e., ticket sales, support facility oversight, etc.). Provide oversight with NCAA mandated Student-Athlete Advisory Committee coordinating their activities and meetings. Assist in the management with, and provide ongoing oversight for, the school and clinic program aimed at community outreach and fundraising. Provide daily oversight and be accountable for all completed intercollegiate team travel including reconciliation forms and roster accountability. Assist in the 24/7 management of athletic recreation facilities. Supervision of marketing and promotions\u2019 intern with emphasis directed on on-going student attendance, loyalty rewards program and fan engagement. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Director of Intercollegiate Athletics, and Recreation. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Good interpersonal and communication skills (written and oral). Ability to work with a diversified population. Strong knowledge and ability with computers and web-based programs. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor\u2019s Degree. Experience: At least four years\u2019 experience gained by working in a college or university environment. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s Degree in physical education, recreation, sports administration, or related field. Bilingual. Does this position have Direct Reports? No Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 10NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $60,000 - $66,000 Work Schedule Non-Standard Work Week. Nights and weekends required. Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Director of Athletics and Executive Director of the Anchor Fund Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Continuing End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit PSA Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 10/02/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor's degree? Yes No * Do you have at least four years of experience gained by working in a college or university environment? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11334": {"title": "Adjuncts, First-Year Writing (Composition/Rhetoric)", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjuncts, First-Year Writing (Composition/Rhetoric) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjuncts, First-Year Writing (Composition/Rhetoric) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC/AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld. There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available . Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1,683/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjuncts, First-Year Writing (Composition/Rhetoric) Department Name First Year Writing Program Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Faculty of Arts and Science Position Overview The English Department is seeking candidates to fill part-time instructor positions for First Year Writing courses. We welcome applications from those qualified to teach introductory, intermediate and advanced courses. We seek adjunct faculty committed to teaching and working with our multicultural student population, teaching courses as needed at the undergraduate level. Essential Duties * Teach courses as needed at the undergraduate level. Occasional Duties N/A Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Qualifications Master\u2019s Degree, ABD or Doctorate in Composition, Rhetoric, Writing Studies, or related field. Minimum of three years of experience teaching writing at the postsecondary level along with significant coursework in Composition, Rhetoric, or Writing Studies at the Master\u2019s level. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience at the college level. Experience teaching multilingual writers. Bilingual. Environmental Conditions Teaching/instruction is performed in a traditional classroom setting. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00034 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available Multiple Anticipated Start Date or Semester Academic 2026 Posting Date 07/16/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC / AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld. There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available . Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11327": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty, School of Business (2026)", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty, School of Business (2026) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjunct Faculty, School of Business (2026) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC/AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld. There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available . Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1,683/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjunct Faculty, School of Business (2026) Department Name School of Business Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Other Position Overview To teach the BUS 100 course which prepares students for the college experience, builds professional and technical skills, and introduces students in business careers. Course content includes the Microsoft Office Suite including Word, Power Point, Excel, and then builds learning skills including time management, navigating a learning management platform, and study skills, and begins to develop professional skills including interpersonal communication, writing, customer service, teamwork, and problem solving. The course integrates engaging learning modalities including guest speakers, group activities, case studies. Essential Duties Prepare students for the college experience. Begin to develop skills in technology. Build professional skills. Introduce students to majors and careers in business. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Dean, School of business. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities n/a Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in a business discipline. Professional experience in business and some teaching experience at the college level. Preferred Qualifications Candidate must be able to teach the Microsoft Office Suite including Word, PowerPoint, and Excel and be an engaging, interactive teacher who can motivate Freshman to be curious learners and succeed academically. Candidate should have knowledge of customer service principles and possess strong presentation skills. Candidate should be willing and able to mentor and coach students. Environmental Conditions This is an in person class taught in a RIC classroom. Candidates should be able to navigate the RIC learning platform Blackboard. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00054 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available 1 Anticipated Start Date or Semester 2026 Posting Date 09/08/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC / AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld. There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available . Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11322": {"title": "Adjunct, Department of Special Education", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjunct, Department of Special Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjunct, Department of Special Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis as instructional and supervisory needs arise. The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development welcomes applications from individuals committed to excellence in teaching, mentoring, supervision, and professional preparation. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1,683/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjunct, Department of Special Education Department Name Special Education Department Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Feinstein School of Education and Human Development Position Overview The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development ( FSEHD ) at Rhode Island College prepares educators, counselors, school psychologists, wellness and exercise science, and youth development professionals who positively impact schools, communities, and the lives of children, youth, and adults. The FSEHD is committed to excellence, equity, inclusion, community engagement, and preparing highly qualified professionals throughout Rhode Island and beyond. The FSEHD invites applications from qualified professionals interested in serving as adjunct faculty teaching content, practicum, or seminar courses and/or supervising student teachers or interns across its undergraduate and graduate programs. Essential Duties Department of Special Education \u2013 Programs: Special Education Undergraduate Program Early Childhood Special Education Graduate Programs in Special Education Assignments may include: Teaching undergraduate or graduate content courses Teaching practicum, internship, or seminar courses Serving as a college supervisor. Supervising student teachers or interns in PK-12 settings or counseling, youth development, or wellness and exercise community organizations. Contact: Cara McDermott, Chair of the Special Education Department. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Dean of the FSEHD . Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree. Relevant professional experience in the field. Experience working with diverse learners and communities. Strong communication, mentoring, and supervisory skills. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate Degree preferred. Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00066 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available Multiple Anticipated Start Date or Semester Posting Date 07/08/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis as instructional and supervisory needs arise. The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development welcomes applications from individuals committed to excellence in teaching, mentoring, supervision, and professional preparation. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11279": {"title": "Senior Programmer Analyst", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Senior Programmer Analyst Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Senior Programmer Analyst Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the United States without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00887 Position Title Senior Programmer Analyst Division Administration and Finance Division Department Name Information Technology Services Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview The Senior Programmer Analyst supports Rhode Island College\u2019s Enterprise Information Services team by designing, developing, maintaining, and integrating applications and technology solutions that support campus operations. The role involves programming, system analysis, testing, troubleshooting, documentation, and providing technical guidance to campus stakeholders. The ideal candidate will have at least four years of programming experience, with strong skills in SQL /PL- SQL , relational databases, and other programming or scripting languages. They should be analytical, detail-oriented, customer-focused, and comfortable working both independently and collaboratively. Experience with SaaS applications, Oracle PeopleSoft or similar ERP systems, iPaaS solutions, Microsoft SQL /Oracle databases, and higher education technology is preferred. Primary Purpose Design, develop, and maintain applications in support of College administrative and academic objectives. Develop specifications for other programmer/analysts and work from specifications supplied by others. May have project and related supervisory responsibilities. Essential Duties Define system requirements with user departments. Prepare feasibility studies of new systems. Define program specifications and systems procedures. Participate in evaluating application software used to support administrative systems. Develop applications and track changes and updates. Develop new programs and modify existing programs according to specifications and department standards. Test applications and evaluate system performance before implementation. Develop, and maintain application development documents in accordance with department standards. Review applications and documentation developed by other team members to ensure the compliance with application development specifications and standards. Provide training to users on functions of new systems. Maintain proficiency in programming, systems analysis and project control tools and techniques used to develop administrative systems. Perform duties and responsibilities of a Programmer/Analyst. Assist in identifying user needs, making system presentations, integrating individual systems into major institutional systems, establishing and enforcing standards, training staff, and assigning programs. Evaluate, specify, and procure related components. Assist in developing information technology related bids, contracts, request for proposals and vendor relationships in support of information technology initiatives. Participate in committees, working groups, councils, etc. in support of information technology initiatives. Function independently or as a member of an information technology team as assigned. Lead, manage, and supervise technical, professional clerical, and student support staff as assigned. As part of self-training and in support of comprehensive, redundant, user focused support, perform functions normally assigned to other information technology support staff as required. Consistently develop and exhibit a positive, user focused, customer service attitude, and atmosphere. Work with the campus community, vendors, and IS professionals to achieve College objectives. Provide related administrative functions and help desk support, as required. Provide on call remote or on-campus support for any job-related issues, as required. Work occasional evenings, weekends, and/or holidays, as required. Occasional Duties Perform other related duties as assigned by the Director. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Competence in Microsoft Windows system platform. Competence in SQL and in at least two programming languages. Understanding of programming logic and competence in application design. Project management skills and ability to work with other professional staff. Ability to interpret institutional policies, plans, objectives, rules and regulations and communicate the interpretation to subordinates and others. Ability to communicate effectively (verbally and in writing) and possess strong interpersonal skills. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor\u2019s Degree. Experience: A minimum of four years of programming experience, including experience with SQL , at least two programming languages, and the Windows system platform. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s in CS, CIS , Accounting, or closely related field. Experience in SQL and in using one or more programming languages such as: Java, PeopleSoft, SQL , SQR , Visual Basic, etc. Experience in supporting ERP or administrative systems such as HR, Payroll, Student Administration, Financial, etc. Understanding of financial systems and some core financial processes. Experience in PeopleSoft (especially PeopleSoft Financials). Experience in Microsoft SQL Database and/or Oracle Database. Experience in higher education. Does this position have Direct Reports? No Environmental Conditions This position requires occasional lifting, moving, and or installation of moderately heavy equipment (such as computers), wiring, and other related information technology components. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 12NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $85,000 - $95,000 Work Schedule Full-Time, 35 hours per week. Monday \u2013 Friday 8:30AM \u2013 4:30PM May be required to work outside of normal business hours based on departmental needs. Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Director, Enterprise Information Services Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Continuing End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit PSA Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 09/16/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the United States without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have an Bachelor's Degree? Yes No Do you have four years of programming experience, including experience with SQL, at least two programming languages, and the Windows system platform? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11392": {"title": "Associate Director of Admissions Operations", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Associate Director of Admissions Operations Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Associate Director of Admissions Operations Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00900 Position Title Associate Director of Admissions Operations Division Student Success Division Department Name Admissions Office Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview The Associate Director of Admissions Operations will provide strategic leadership and oversight of admissions data, technology, and operational processes to support the College\u2019s undergraduate enrollment goals. This role manages the Slate CRM and its integration with the College\u2019s student information system, ensuring data integrity, accurate reporting, and efficient information flow across departments. The Associate Director leads the development and implementation of data-driven strategies, communication plans, recruitment initiatives, and process improvements to enhance the student recruitment and enrollment experience. Additionally, this position oversees admissions reporting and analysis, identifies opportunities to improve enrollment outcomes, and promotes the effective use of technology and industry best practices. Through collaboration with campus partners, MIS , and admissions leadership, the Associate Director supports strategic decision-making, operational efficiency, and continuous improvement. The role also supervises admissions staff, coordinates key enrollment initiatives, and helps advance the College\u2019s efforts to attract, engage, and enroll prospective students. Primary Purpose The Associate Director of Admissions Operations provides leadership and strategic direction for the Office of Undergraduate Admission as it relates to data integrity, data collection, analysis, usage, and presentation. The Associate Director of Admissions Operations is a member of the leadership team, and provides training and support for all things related to admission-data and technology, such as Slate CRM and the College\u2019s student information system, while assisting with the execution of data-driven processes, communication plans, outreach efforts, reporting and analysis. The Associate Director is responsible for ensuring the seamless flow of data between Slate and the College\u2019s student information system through close collaboration with MIS and various departments throughout the College. The Associate Director will be goal-driven, analytical, and responsible for continued evolution and modernization of the Office of Undergraduate Admissions practices, operations, and technology utilization and integration. A forward thinker, the Associate Director of Admissions Operations will ensure full utilization of the Slate CRM platform, and incorporate industry best practices to develop and implement solutions involving process design, data information, and operational procedures. The Associate Director of Admissions Operations will play a vital role in promoting the College and attracting new students by working closely with the College community. Essential Duties Lead the development, management, and maintenance of Slate CRM and coordinate integrations with MIS in the College\u2019s student information system and other technology applications. Oversee the input of prospect, inquiry, and application data into the CRM and data management system, maintaining a focus on data integrity and accuracy at all times. Advise on and execute the program-level vision, strategy, key performance indicators, and goals as determined by the Director and Dean. Manage operational and data aspects of the undergraduate admission process, including but not limited to: prospect maintenance, application management, documentation collection, data importing and exporting, decision processing, travel planning, and communication campaigns. Supervise communication flows, including timely and accurate processing of all application materials and decisions, and assist as needed with implementation of additional communication campaigns. Monitor, maintain and make recommendations for data collection updates and user enhancements to the admission transactional pages on the external website. Create and maintain business processes across the department involving system tracked information, such as admission inquiries and applications, admission file review and decision notification, financial aid awarding, and enrollment deposits. Collaborate with MIS , develop intuitive interface designs for end-users and continuous staff training and professional development to maximize CRM functionality. Lead operational efforts focused on quality assurance, increased efficiency, and cost reduction. Coordinate logistics for new student enrollment efforts involving multiple functional units and help drive related projects toward completion. Oversee data processing and sound data management in collaboration with staff in other enrollment management units, cross-campus partners, and external partners (e.g. vendors). Develop, coordinate and prepare statistical admissions reports and data analysis. Assist in delivering regular enrollment data reports and fulfill ad-hoc data requests. Serve as a project manager for strategic operational initiatives as assigned. Maintain partnerships at the national, state, and local levels, including with key professional and industry organizations. Work closely with the Director and/or Dean on the development and implementation of new student enrollment goals and recruitment strategies. Work closely with the director to manage complex information and data which enhances the recruitment and yield efforts of the College. In conjunction with the Admission Leadership Team, recommend strategies and plans to address opportunities and gaps in the enrollment funnel with the aim of increasing activity, engagement, volume and conversion. Supervise Admissions team members. Occasional Duties Assist at all major recruitment events. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Administrative experience implementing, training, and managing CRM /database systems. Able to be an agent of change in a rapidly changing environment. Proven ability to analyze data to identify trends and drive innovation within the related field. Detail oriented, able to multi-task and work under pressure. Demonstrated strong interpersonal, verbal and written communication skills. Demonstrated supervisory experience. Demonstrated ability to work independently and as part of a team. Evidence of commitment to professional growth and development. Flexibility, dedication, initiative, confidentiality, and the ability to learn are expected. Demonstrate acute attention to detail, strong organization and problem-solving abilities. Required Qualifications Education: Master\u2019s Degree. Experience: 5-7 years of progressively responsible, full-time experience in higher education college admissions, financial aid, or other enrollment management units, including experience with diverse populations. Experience managing a CRM . Experience integrating a CRM and student information system. Experience mining system data and producing high-level reporting and analysis. Supervisory experience managing/directing staff groups or teams. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of Slate CRM , and MS Professional software packages are beneficial, as well as the ability to leverage CRM technology to identify and implement efficiencies and measure outcomes. Demonstrated familiarity with the undergraduate programs at RIC . Bilingual in English/Spanish (fluent in speaking and writing). Does this position have Direct Reports? Yes Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 14NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $80,000-$90,000 Work Schedule Monday through Friday, 8:30am-4:30pm; some evening and weekend responsibilities. Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Director, Outreach and Recruitment (Admissions)/Alum Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Continuing End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit PSA Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 10/16/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master's Degree? Yes No * Do you 5-7 years of progressively responsible, full-time experience in higher education college admissions, financial aid, or other enrollment management units, including experience with diverse populations? Yes No * Do you have experience managing, and integrating a CRM and student information system? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11191": {"title": "Assistive Technology Specialist", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Assistive Technology Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Assistive Technology Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00868 Position Title Assistive Technology Specialist Division Academic Affairs Division Department Name Sherlock Center on Disabilities Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview The Assistive Technology Specialist provides technical assistance, training, and support to help individuals with intellectual and developmental disabilities access and effectively use assistive technology. Working through the Sherlock Center\u2019s statewide initiatives, this position assesses community needs, develops accessible resources and training opportunities, promotes evidence-based practices, and collaborates with schools, agencies, families, and community partners to expand access to assistive technology services and supports. The ideal candidate will have advanced training in assistive technology, experience supporting individuals with intellectual and developmental disabilities, strong communication and collaboration skills, and a commitment to person-centered and independent living principles. Bilingual candidates, particularly those fluent in Spanish or Portuguese, are encouraged to apply. Primary Purpose Provide technical assistance and support to the Sherlock Center\u2019s life span initiatives related to supporting individuals with developmental disabilities to access and use technology. This includes identifying statewide initiatives, supporting the development of a statewide approach to supporting technology initiatives, including training, and assistive technology (AT). Essential Duties Assess the collective needs of people with disabilities in Rhode Island and identify programs and support for them to access the assistive technology (AT) that can help them meet their goals. Participate in the planning, organization, implementation, and evaluation of statewide learning opportunities for the disability community across all ages. Research policies and practices that affect access to assistive technology, and advocate for access to assistive technology devices and services. Work with other agencies to increase the capacity of public and private entities to provide assistive technology assistance. Identify funding sources to support assistive technology use and training activities. Develop accessible technical assistance and guidance resources and documents for use in implementing evidence-based practices. Provide technical assistance to local service areas at the state, regional, and local levels for the purposes of: (1) assisting service areas in coming into compliance with federal regulations and state policy and (2) supporting the implementation of family-centered service systems that promote maximum developmental outcomes for children. Provide training and technical assistance within the structures of state and local agency systems of personnel development, at statewide and regional conferences, and at designated training events. Make presentations to public groups about assistive technology and related issues. Perform outreach activities focused on difficult to reach and underserved populations. Develop collaborative relationships with other agencies to facilitate cross-disability, consumer-responsive delivery of assistive technology services. Document and compile technology use data, as needed, to support documentation in annual reports. Compile and maintain, resource information on products, directions for use, maintenance and funding sources for such products/devices; computerize this information to facilitate updating. Prepare information sheets and brochures in accessible formats, which make this information readily available to the public Serve as local liaison to school districts, state agencies and organizations for Sherlock Center Assistive Technology Project activities. Attend regular staff meetings and training opportunities. Use the Independent Living Philosophy to guide and model all activities, communication, and developed materials. Occasional Duties Other duties as may be assigned by the Executive Director of the Sherlock Center. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Essential knowledge and specialized subject knowledge required to perform the essential functions of the job. Working knowledge of the principles, practices, and ethical standards of AT; relevant state and federal laws, rules and regulations; and applicable district policies and procedures. Knowledge of, or willingness to learn, assistive technology (e.g., hardware, software, 3-D printing, smart home, safety, and security supports). Ability to apply established technology solutions to enhance individual or small work group efficiency and effectiveness. Responsible for orienting and training others. Ability to effectively communicate with district personnel, schools, the community, and families. Exceptional listening, verbal, and written communications skills. Excellent customer service skills. Great attention to detail and organizational skills. Computer proficiency in Microsoft Suite including Word, Excel, and PowerPoint as well as software applications relevant to area of responsibility. Ability to work well independently and in a team setting. Ability to consult with individuals in the disability community including school, provider in developing and implementing effective interventions for individuals using AT. Required Qualifications Master\u2019s Degree in a major field of study or degree emphasis in Special Education or a Related Service. Advanced training in Assistive Technology. Experience with people with Intellectual and Developmental Disabilities ( IDD ). Preferred Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s Degree with a minimum of 5 year\u2019s of experience supporting individuals with developmental disabilities with assistive technology. Applicants who have experience supporting individuals with intellectual and/or developmental disabilities. Applicants who are bi-lingual in Spanish and/or Portuguese. Does this position have Direct Reports? No Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 10NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $70,000 Work Schedule Full-Time, 35 hours per week. Monday \u2013 Friday 8:30AM \u2013 4:30PM Work may be required during some evenings and weekends Benefits Full-time employee benefits include: Comprehensive Health Benefits and Rewards for Wellness Incentives Generous Paid Time Off Family/Parental Leave Tuition Waivers at RIC , CCRI & URI Retirement Plan Long-term Disability Coverage Variety of voluntary add-on\u2019s For a complete listing, visit: http://www.employeebenefits.ri.gov/benefits/new/index.php Reports To (Title) Executive Director of Paul V. Sherlock Center on Disabilities Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Grant-funded End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit Non-union Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 07/07/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master's Degree in a major field of study or degree emphasis in Special Education or a Related Service. yes no * Do you have advanced training in Assistive Technology? yes no * Do you have experience with people with Intellectual and Developmental Disabilities (IDD)? yes no Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/10999": {"title": "Technical Assistance Specialist, Adult Services", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Technical Assistance Specialist, Adult Services Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Technical Assistance Specialist, Adult Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00836 Position Title Technical Assistance Specialist, Adult Services Division Academic Affairs Division Department Name Sherlock Center on Disabilities Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview The Paul V. Sherlock Center on Disabilities at Rhode Island College seeks a Technical Assistance Specialist to lead grant\u2011funded initiatives focused on improving systems of support for adults with disabilities , including individuals with IDD and co\u2011occurring needs. This role leads the design and delivery of statewide and national training and technical assistance , grounded in adult learning theory and evidence\u2011based practices. The TA Specialist collaborates with individuals with lived experience, families, direct support professionals, service providers, and state leaders to strengthen outcomes across key adult life domains such as community living, employment, health and wellness, safety, social inclusion, and advocacy. Responsibilities include developing and implementing multi\u2011year programs, delivering webinars and in\u2011person trainings, overseeing project logistics and staff support, participating in evaluation and data collection, and disseminating project outcomes through presentations and publications. This position is ideal for a collaborative, self\u2011directed professional committed to person\u2011centered practices, system improvement, and advancing equity and inclusion for adults with disabilities. Primary Purpose This full-time, grant-funded position is located at the Paul V. Sherlock Center on Disabilities. The position scope involves leading projects within the Sherlock Center\u2019s adult program area. The Technical Assistance (TA) Specialist will provide training and technical assistance to the disability community related to the needs of adults with disabilities, including people with IDD who have co-occurring physical, mental, or age-related needs. Areas of adult focus include the life domains of community living, employment, healthy living, safety & security, social & spirituality, and advocacy & engagement. Essential Duties Apply research\u2010based practices of instructional design and adult learning theory using the necessary tools to create a high\u2010quality training program and implement those practices (including but not limited to learning activities, training content and assignments, and participant knowledge and/or skill assessments). Collaborate with stakeholders on the design of education and training program and technical assistance as directed by grants and program objectives. Collaborate with local/state leadership personnel and advisory boards related to project activities and outcomes. Lead statewide and national implementation of programs from the Sherlock Center that include evaluating needs and exercising professional judgement to tailor training and technical assistance offerings to best serve stakeholders. Participate in data collection needed for the evaluation of program implementation. Plan, design, and deliver webinars, conference calls, and in\u2010person meetings for members of the disability community including individuals with lived experience, family members, direct support personnel, and professionals. Disseminate information on project activities/outcomes, including but not limited to preparing blogs, newsletters, conference presentations, and poster sessions. Direct the work of staff with regards to logistics, promotion, and training needs of each program. Assist with research and data collection activities as required by project. Travel to residences and other community locations for meetings and project activities. Occasional Duties Other duties as may be assigned by the Executive Director of the Sherlock Center. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Demonstrated ability to develop, implement, and evaluate multi-year programs and services for new and existing projects and contracts. Demonstrated experience working with Direct Support and other Professionals within disability services and supports. Demonstrated experience working with individuals with IDD . Knowledge of key issues, evidenced-based best practices, and resources in community living and employment policy and practice issues related to long-term services and supports for persons with IDD , such as workforce recruitment and retention challenges. Knowledge of the life domains including community living, employment, healthy living, safety & security, social & spirituality, and advocacy & engagement. Knowledge of person-centered thinking, and self-determination. Ability to work independently and as part of a diverse team across multiple settings and initiatives in a collaborative environment. Demonstrated ability to communicate clearly and concisely with people of diverse backgrounds and levels of authority. Demonstrated proficiency in writing and presentation skills. Demonstrated experience in guiding, supporting and directing the work of others. Experience working in diverse communities. Required Qualifications Education: BA/BS degree Experience : 4 years\u2019 experience in human services, business, education, evaluation & measurement, public health, psychology, social work, or related discipline. In lieu of an academic degree, at least 4 years of work experience in human services for people with disabilities that includes directing and managing complex, multi-year projects or activities. Preferred Qualifications N/A Does this position have Direct Reports? No Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 10NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range 56,000-62,000 Work Schedule Monday \u2013 Friday 8:30-4:30 Some evenings and weekends Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Associate Director, Adult Services Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Grant-funded End of Temporary or Limited Position 06/19/2027 Collective Bargaining Unit Non-union Posting Information Number of Positions Available 3 Application Open Date 03/31/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor's Degree in Special Education, Vocational Rehabilitation, Supported Employment or a related field? Yes No * Do you have five years experience providing or coordinating services and supports to individuals with disabilities? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11379": {"title": "Degree Audit and Graduation Specialist", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Degree Audit and Graduation Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Degree Audit and Graduation Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. The College requires that all applicants and employees be able to perform the essential functions of the job and will explore reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00896 Position Title Degree Audit and Graduation Specialist Division Student Success Division Department Name Office of the Registrar Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview Reporting to the Assistant Registrar, the Degree Audit and Graduation Specialist supports student progress and success by managing the PeopleSoft academic advisement system and ensuring accurate degree audits, academic program requirements, and student records. The position monitors student progress toward degree completion, conducts final degree audits, processes graduation applications, and supports graduation and commencement activities. The specialist serves as a key resource for students, faculty, advisors, and administrators by interpreting academic requirements, policies, and procedures and resolving individual student issues. The role also requires maintaining confidentiality and compliance with FERPA while providing timely, professional, and customer-focused support to the college community. Primary Purpose The Degree Audit and Graduation Specialist will manage the PeopleSoft academic advisement module including building, implementation and maintenance of programs, majors, minors for all students. Monitor student progress toward degree completion and conduct the final degree audit. Administer academic policies related to graduation honors, academic dismissal and probation. Provide information on college policies and procedures to students, faculty, administrative offices and other members of the college community. Essential Duties Build, implement, and maintain the College\u2019s Student Information System \u2013 PeopleSoft\u2019s academic advisement module and ensure all assigned academic advisement reports (AARs) are accurate and up-to-date. Monitor student degree audits from matriculation to completion (additions, course substitutions, change of major, withdrawals, failures, etc.). Perform final degree audits and confirm eligibility for students who apply for graduation, providing notification of any outstanding degree requirements to both the student and advisor. Meet with students who have questions or concerns about their audit and progress towards graduation. Process graduation applications for assigned students and regularly provide graduation list updates to the Registrar. Assist academic advisors, chairs, faculty, staff and students on how to read, interpret and use the academic advisement report including degree, major, and general education requirements. Provide effective and timely communication and customer service to all constituents by responding promptly and professionally to inquiries received via email, phone, or in person from students, faculty, and staff. Research, address and provide timely follow-up with students, advisors, chairs and deans regarding individual student issues/situations. Responsible for properly maintaining student and academic records in the College\u2019s SIS \u2013 PeopleSoft. Stay informed of curriculum changes per academic affairs, and monitor effective dates and catalog changes to regularly apply changes/criteria that will best serve students. Support the Registrar\u2019s office with all graduation and commencement activities. Maintain confidentiality of student records and meetings with students in accordance with FERPA laws and regulations. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Assistant Registrar and/or Registrar. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Fundamental understanding of FERPA laws and regulations. Proficient computer skills. Excellent communication skills (both written and oral) and effective interpersonal skills. Demonstrated analytical, planning and organizational skills. Ability to work well with a variety of campus personnel, and function in a team-oriented environment. Demonstrated commitment to student success and a student-centered approach to providing service and resolving student issues. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor\u2019s degree. Experience : Two years of experience with records, registrar, and/or academic advising in a higher education institution. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree. Experience with student system degree audit modules such as PeopleSoft. Does this position have Direct Reports? No Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 12NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $70,000-75,000 Work Schedule Monday-Friday 8:30am \u2013 4:30pm Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Registrar Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Continuing End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit PSA Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 10/09/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. The College requires that all applicants and employees be able to perform the essential functions of the job and will explore reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned bachelor's degree? yes no * Do you have two years of experience with records, registrar, and/or academic advising in a higher education institution? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/10364": {"title": "Residential Tutor Counselor", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Residential Tutor Counselor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Residential Tutor Counselor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The number of available positions is contingent on student enrollment and funding. Candidates must upload a resume, cover letter, and the most recent unofficial transcript, in addition to providing three references. In the cover letter, identify three subjects from the Required Qualifications that the candidate is qualified to tutor. A Tutor Counselor may be assigned to tutor up to three classes. Salary range: $3,000 to $4,000 (all applicable taxes will be deducted). Board: will be provided Monday through Friday (excluding July 6). Housing will be available for the duration of employment. Fringe benefits include health insurance, which will only be available from June 29 to August 7 and will be secondary to the employee\u2019s health plan. Applicants offered a Tutor Counselor position must submit their official college transcript in a sealed envelope by May 29th. Foreign citizens working in the U.S. under a visa should note that this is a short-term position, and Rhode Island College will not sponsor any type of work-authorization visa. Before finalizing employment, this position requires successful completion of a background check, which may include, but is not limited to, verification of education, employment history, and a criminal and sex offender record check. The employee must also submit specific forms required by the RI College Human Resources Office. Posting Details Posting Detail Information Posting Number NT00127 Position Title/Assigment Residential Tutor Counselor Department Name Position Type Staff - Casual Position Description Posting Information Number of Positions Available Benefits Eligible? No Application Open Date 02/18/2026 Additional Information The number of available positions is contingent on student enrollment and funding. Candidates must upload a resume, cover letter, and the most recent unofficial transcript, in addition to providing three references. In the cover letter, identify three subjects from the Required Qualifications that the candidate is qualified to tutor. A Tutor Counselor may be assigned to tutor up to three classes. Salary range: $3,000 to $4,000 (all applicable taxes will be deducted). Board: will be provided Monday through Friday (excluding July 6). Housing will be available for the duration of employment. Fringe benefits include health insurance, which will only be available from June 29 to August 7 and will be secondary to the employee\u2019s health plan. Applicants offered a Tutor Counselor position must submit their official college transcript in a sealed envelope by May 29th. Foreign citizens working in the U.S. under a visa should note that this is a short-term position, and Rhode Island College will not sponsor any type of work-authorization visa. Before finalizing employment, this position requires successful completion of a background check, which may include, but is not limited to, verification of education, employment history, and a criminal and sex offender record check. The employee must also submit specific forms required by the RI College Human Resources Office. EEO Statement As an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity institution that values and is committed to inclusion and expanding the diversity of its faculty and staff, the College invites members of protected classes, including minorities and persons with disabilities, to identify themselves as such at the time of application. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you available to meet the required time and commitments outlines in this summer job description? Yes No * Do you have prior work experience as a resident assistant in a college residence hall, counselor in youth programs, summer camps, mentor, or tutor/peer advisor? Yes No * Had you earned a minimum of 30 college credits and a minimum GPA of 2.75 as the end of the previous fall semester? Yes No * If you are currently a student in the US under a visa, is your employment eligibility restricted to a specific institution other than RI College? (The position you are applying for is a short term position and Rhode Island College will not sponsor a work-authorization visa). If you are not under a Visa, answer no to this question. yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document (see special instructions) Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11358": {"title": "Admissions Reader", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Admissions Reader Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Admissions Reader Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is part of a career ladder, giving you the opportunity to advance to higher level roles as you gain experience and obtain the required qualifications. Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00895 Position Title Admissions Reader Division Student Success Division Department Name Admissions Office Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview The Admissions Officer will recruit, interview and advise prospective students as well as read and evaluate applications for admissions decisions including traditional and non-traditional admission programs. Primary Purpose The Admissions Reader will perform outreach and recruitment including, but not limited to fall and spring recruitment travel, counseling prospective students and families throughout the college application, selection, and enrollment process; assisting guidance professionals, faculty, alumni/ae, and prospective students and families to better understand the college\u2019s mission through personal interviews, group presentations, and extensive follow-up communication; while representing the college with the utmost of professionalism. Essential Duties Develop a working knowledge and remain current on all College recruitment messages, facts, and policies. Recruit prospective students and conduct extensive follow-up communication and tracking. Manages a recruitment territory and associated contacts by identifying, scheduling, and visiting targeted high schools and two-year colleges. Represent the College at all recruitment events assigned. Participate in Counselor-of-the-Day responsibilities by delivering engaging presentations for prospective students, families, and guests. Conduct thorough application review of admissions materials and provide decisions in a timely fashion. Enter data into and use the CRM to support recruitment, tracking and communication with prospective students. Collaborate with other administrative offices, academic departments, committees and College personnel to effectively support student recruitment and enrollment. Travel extensively in-state and out-of-state, with evening and weekend work required. Be an active and positive member of the admissions team, demonstrating a willingness to participate and volunteer in team initiatives. Occasional Duties Travel in-state and out-of-state and some non-standard work hours. Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Associate Director of Admissions. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Excellent communication (oral and written), interpersonal, organizational and basic computer skills. Ability to represent the College effectively and to interact with individuals and groups in an articulate, sensitive, persuasive, and professional manner. Sensitivity to the needs of minority students and other special groups, including non-traditional students. Commitment to professional growth and development in college admissions. Capability and willingness to travel and work nonstandard hours. Must be able to arrange transportation for daily, in-state travel and for out-of-state recruitment travel as needed. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor\u2019s degree. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated familiarity with the undergraduate programs at RIC . Previous post-baccalaureate professional experience in college/university level admissions. Bilingual in Spanish (fluent in speaking and writing). Does this position have Direct Reports? No Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 9NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $53,000-$67,000 Work Schedule Full-time, Calendar Year Appointment, Non Standard hours, evenings and weekends Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Associate Director of Admissions Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Continuing End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit PSA Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 09/30/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions This position is part of a career ladder, giving you the opportunity to advance to higher level roles as you gain experience and obtain the required qualifications. Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement As an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity institution that values and is committed to inclusion and to expanding the diversity of its faculty and staff, the College invites members of protected classes, including minorities and persons with disabilities, to identify themselves as such at the time of application. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned bachelor's degree? yes no * Do you have demonstrated experience working with SLATE CRM? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11329": {"title": "Adjuncts, Biology Department (Anatomy and Physiology) (2026)", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjuncts, Biology Department (Anatomy and Physiology) (2026) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjuncts, Biology Department (Anatomy and Physiology) (2026) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC/AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld. There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available . Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1,683/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjuncts, Biology Department (Anatomy and Physiology) (2026) Department Name Biology Department Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Faculty of Arts and Science Position Overview The Biology Department is seeking candidates to fill part-time instructor positions with expertise in Anatomy and Physiology. We welcome applications from those qualified to teach introductory, intermediate and advanced courses. We seek adjunct faculty committed to teaching and working with our multicultural student population, teaching courses as needed at the undergraduate/graduate level. Essential Duties Teach in-person specialty classes populated by students majoring in the following areas: Biology, Health Sciences, Nursing: this includes the new Anatomy & Physiology. Occasional Duties Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Qualifications M.A. in a biological science Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate instruction and to mentoring students Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching introductory biology and advanced courses including human anatomy and physiology. Experience with nontraditional students and with an ethnically-diverse student population Environmental Conditions Teaching/instruction is performed in a traditional classroom setting. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00052 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available Multiple Anticipated Start Date or Semester Fall 2026 Posting Date 05/07/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC / AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld. There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available . Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11324": {"title": "Adjuncts, Sociology Department (Sociology and Justice Studies)", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjuncts, Sociology Department (Sociology and Justice Studies) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjuncts, Sociology Department (Sociology and Justice Studies) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC/AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive year (Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld.) There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available . Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1,683/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjuncts, Sociology Department (Sociology and Justice Studies) Department Name Sociology Department Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Faculty of Arts and Science Position Overview The Sociology Department is seeking candidates to fill part-time instructor positions. We welcome applications from those qualified to teach introductory, intermediate and advanced courses in Sociology and in Justice Studies. Essential Duties Teach courses as needed at the undergraduate and graduate levels (with PhD), including some combination of courses in the Sociology, Justice Studies, and Aging Studies curriculum. Teach foundational sociology and justice studies courses, such as Introduction to Sociology and Crime and Criminal Justice, theory, or research methods. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Sociology department chair. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Experience working with nontraditional students and with an ethnically diverse student population. Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate instruction and to mentoring students. Interest in and experience with active and experiential learning. Required Qualifications Masters or Doctoral degree in Sociology, Criminology, Demography or a closely related field. Preferred Qualifications Environmental Conditions Teaching/instruction is performed in a traditional classroom setting with possible options for hybrid and very occasional online formats. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00062 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available Multiple Anticipated Start Date or Semester Posting Date 06/18/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC / AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive year (Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld.) There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available . Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have a Masters or Doctoral degree in Sociology, Criminology, Demography or a closely related field? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11319": {"title": "Adjunct, Department of Health and Physical Education", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjunct, Department of Health and Physical Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjunct, Department of Health and Physical Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis as instructional and supervisory needs arise. The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development welcomes applications from individuals committed to excellence in teaching, mentoring, supervision, and professional preparation. You will be prompted to upload a copy of your educator certification. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1,683/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjunct, Department of Health and Physical Education Department Name Health and Physical Education Department Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Feinstein School of Education and Human Development Position Overview The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development ( FSEHD ) at Rhode Island College prepares educators, counselors, school psychologists, wellness and exercise science, and youth development professionals who positively impact schools, communities, and the lives of children, youth, and adults. The FSEHD is committed to excellence, equity, inclusion, community engagement, and preparing highly qualified professionals throughout Rhode Island and beyond. The FSEHD invites applications from qualified professionals interested in serving as adjunct faculty teaching content, practicum, or seminar courses and/or supervising student teachers or interns across its undergraduate and graduate programs. Essential Duties Department of Health and Physical Education \u2013 Programs: Health Education, Physical Education and Adapted Physical Education Wellness and Exercise Science Assignments may include: Teaching undergraduate or graduate content courses. Teaching practicum, internship, or seminar courses. Serving as a college supervisor. Supervising student teachers or interns in PK-12 settings or counseling, youth development, or wellness and exercise community organizations. Contact: Susan Clark, Chair of the HPE Department. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Dean of the FSEHD . Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree. Relevant professional experience in the field. Experience working with diverse learners and communities. Strong communication, mentoring, and supervisory skills. Educator Certification. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate Degree preferred. Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00063 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available Multiple Anticipated Start Date or Semester Posting Date 07/01/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis as instructional and supervisory needs arise. The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development welcomes applications from individuals committed to excellence in teaching, mentoring, supervision, and professional preparation. You will be prompted to upload a copy of your educator certification. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document (see special instructions) Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11396": {"title": "Director, Dining and Retail Food Services", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Director, Dining and Retail Food Services Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Director, Dining and Retail Food Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please upload a copy of your current RI Department of Health Food Safety Manager Certification. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00899 Position Title Director, Dining and Retail Food Services Division Administration and Finance Division Department Name Dining Services Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview The Director of Dining and Retail Food Services provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for Rhode Island College\u2019s comprehensive dining and retail food service program, including campus dining, caf\u00e9s, catering, meal plans, convenience retail, vending, and special event concessions. The Director oversees financial planning, purchasing, personnel management, staff development, facilities planning, and food safety compliance while delivering high-quality, customer-focused services that meet the diverse nutritional and dietary needs of the College community. As the College\u2019s primary resource on food and hospitality services, the Director advances innovative, financially responsible programs that enhance the campus experience, support student success, and align with the College\u2019s mission and strategic goals. Primary Purpose The Director of Dining and Retail Food Services is responsible for the efficient and effective administration of all aspects of the dining and retail food operations; serving as the primary source of campus expertise on food and hospitality services; providing vision and leadership in the development of a comprehensive, campus wide food service program which consistently meets the needs and expectations of a diverse college community, while attaining required financial objectives; responsible for establishing and fostering foodservice environments which are aligned with, and contribute to the College\u2019s Strategic Plan, Mission, and Goals. Essential Duties Responsible for developing a comprehensive food service program for a diverse college community, as well as the vision, goals and leadership for successful attainment. Responsible for the management and operations of all Dining Service operations to include Donovan Dining Center, The Beestro Cafe, Catering Services, Vending Services (Managed by a 3rd Party), Mobile and Special Event Concessions, Quick Mart Convenience Store and retail operations as maybe assigned. Responsible for the administration of all Dining Service program components to include Meal Plan Programs, Cash Sales, Catering, retail operations, nutritional services, and Conference and Special Events. Provides leadership in the formation of policies, procedures and operational guidelines for Dining Service with a focus on customer service and student success, while ensuring adherence to applicable standards and budgetary objectives. Responsible for the development and implementation of marketing concepts, services, menus, and pricing guidelines which meet the need and expectations of the College community and positively influence customer satisfaction. Responsible for the development of a Nutritional/Dietary Services program component, supporting the unique and diverse needs of the College community. Responsible for the management and oversight of more than 75, management, administrative support, food service, and housekeeping personnel. Responsible for the identification of workforce needs department-wide, development of job assignments, and plan and direct work of assigned employees in a manner which improves operational effectiveness, customer service, and budgetary objectives. Responsible to implement personnel policies for the department, recommend personnel actions and actively participate in labor relation matters to include all levels of the grievance process. Responsible for the development of a highly proficient, professional, and customer centric work force through leadership and training in key areas including but not limited to food preparation, customer service, sanitation, and safety, etc. Prepare, administer, and monitor annual operating budget(s); prepare timely cost accounting reports analyzing the budget status and implement operational changes to achieve efficiencies and attain budgetary goals. Create and/or monitor computerized sales, menu planning, purchasing, inventory, recipe development, payment and accounting systems to insure operational effectiveness. Establish purchasing standards and procedures for the department and oversee the procurement processes for all College Dining Services food and non-food purchases, ensuring the appropriate integrity and efficiencies. Identify and plan for short and long term renovation, maintenance and new equipment needs for Dining Service facilities, prepare related reports, and participate on facilities and building committees. Evaluate, recommend and oversee branded concepts and/or franchise operations campus wide. Advise the Sr. Director od Auxiliary Services & Operations on the matters pertaining to food service. Function as the College\u2019s liaison for food service information and nutritional needs for students, faculty, staff, guests and other state departments. Serve as the primary designated school official for the USDA Federal Commodities Program, State of RI Food Advisory Panel, the RIDOA Prime Vendor Working Group, and the RIC Food Advisory Committee. Exhibit a commitment to professional growth and development through internal and external associations and committees. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Executive Director of Auxiliary Services and Operations. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Demonstrated knowledge of state purchasing procedures, federal and state health laws. Working knowledge of computerized menu management, access and inventory systems. Working knowledge of computerized ID systems. Working knowledge of computerized financial and personnel systems. Be creative and innovative in thinking and work habits, with a commitment to diversity, customer service, and student success. Proficient with personal computers, printers; word processing, database management and spreadsheet software, including Microsoft Office Systems, CBORD Menu Management System, VISIX , PEOPLESOFT , and POS systems. Ability to represent the College positively and effectively with prospective and current students, faculty, staff, alumni, outside agencies and the public. Ability to provide strong leadership and a clear vision to staff, as well as implement policies and procedures with a focus on customer service and student success. Ability and willingness to develop, maintain, and facilitate professional relationships with all internal and external stakeholders. Ability to effectively organize, prioritize, and multi-task in a high volume, fast paced, fluid environment. Possess and demonstrate excellent interpersonal, analytical, and written/oral communication skills. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Business Administration, Public Administration, or related area. Experience: A minimum of ten years of progressively responsible experience in the management of a large, complex, high-volume food service operation. Demonstrated experience in labor relations, staff development and oversight of more than 50 unionized personnel. Demonstrated experience in renovations, and maintenance related to food service facilities. Demonstrated financial experience successfully administering a budget exceeding 8 million dollars in revenue. Licenses / Certifications Possess and maintain a current RI Department of Health Food Safety Manager Certification. Possess and maintain a valid Driver\u2019s License. Preferred Qualifications Does this position have Direct Reports? Yes Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 16NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $95,000 - $125,000 Work Schedule Full-Time, 35 weekly hours Flexible to meet departmental needs. Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Executive Director of Auxiliary Services and Operations Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Continuing End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit PSA Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 10/16/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please upload a copy of your current RI Department of Health Food Safety Manager Certification. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Business Administration, Public Administration, or related area? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of ten years of progressively responsible experience in the management of a large, complex, high-volume food service operation? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in labor relations, staff development and oversight of more than 50 unionized personnel? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in renovations, and maintenance related to food service facilities? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated financial experience successfully administering a budget exceeding 8 million dollars in revenue? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Document (see special instructions) Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11252": {"title": "Associate Director of the Sherlock Center", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Associate Director of the Sherlock Center Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Associate Director of the Sherlock Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00825 Position Title Associate Director of the Sherlock Center Division Academic Affairs Division Department Name Sherlock Center on Disabilities Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview The Sherlock Cente r, Rhode Island\u2019s federally designated University Center for Excellence in Developmental Disabilities ( UCEDD ), is seeking a dynamic and mission\u2011driven Associate Director to join our leadership team. This is a unique opportunity to help shape statewide impact, strengthen inclusive communities, and guide innovative programs that enhance the lives of individuals with intellectual and developmental disabilities. As a strategic partner to the Executive Director, the Associate Director plays a key role in driving the UCEDD\u2019s mission, ensuring excellence in service delivery, and advancing the initiatives outlined in the UCEDD\u2019s five\u2011year plan. This leader will oversee core operational functions\u2014including staff supervision, program planning, evaluation, and financial stewardship\u2014while cultivating collaborations across agencies, providers, and community stakeholders. The Associate Director will oversee the Sherlock Center\u2019s adult initiatives , including employment, conflict\u2011free case management, self\u2011directed supports, workforce development, and other emerging topics impacting adults with disabilities. Primary Purpose The Associate Director is responsible for assisting the Executive Director in the overall administration of the UCEDD , which includes carrying out the mission, core functions and federal requirements of the UCEDD . The Associate Director will participate in the planning, development, and implementation of operational functions including hiring, supervising and mentoring staff, as well as monitoring, implementing and reporting on the UCEDD\u2019s five-year work plan. Essential Duties \u2022 To serve as an effective member of the Sherlock Center\u2019s leadership team; to exercise initiative consistent with the Sherlock Center\u2019s goals and objectives; to provide effective leadership consistent with UCEDD five-year plan and other project requirements. \u2022 To effectively represent the UCEDD with a wide range of public and private organizations, groups and individuals; to represent the Sherlock Center on committees, boards, and at a variety of public events and activities. \u2022 To assist in overall program planning and development, fiscal integrity, program and staff evaluation. \u2022 To assist in the efficient and effective delivery of a coordinated program of direct or support services. \u2022 To develop and oversee a variety of service contracts and or grants, as required. As assigned, to develop and maintain appropriate information systems and to generate and disseminate analyses, reports and recommendations as required. \u2022 Helps develop processes and procedures to improve the day-to-day management of the UCEDD . \u2022 Exercises supervisory authority, including hiring, transferring, suspending, promoting, managing conduct and performance, discharging, assigning, rewarding, disciplining, and/or approving hours worked of at least 20 full-time equivalent ( FTE ) employees. \u2022 Ensures that related policies, procedures, and standards are maintained. \u2022 Contributes to the core functions of the UCEDD , including activities of training/teaching, conducting research, disseminating evidence and best practices, and demonstrating model services. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Executive Director of the Sherlock Center. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Knowledge of teaching strategies that promote the participation of individuals who have complex developmental or other disabilities. Knowledge of culturally responsive approaches to informing, supporting and engaging diverse populations or communities, including individuals with complex developmental or other disabilities Knowledge of best practices for implementing project evaluation activities. Excellent written, verbal communication and organizational skills. Excellent computer skills including use of basic word processing and data programs as well as competence in data analysis. Ability to translate research and educational materials into plain language. Ability to prioritize, manage and execute multiple projects concurrently. Proven ability to plan, coordinate, direct and control several functions and programs of a large agency or complex program within the disability community. Proven ability to develop and oversee operating systems including the ability manage a program of fiscal integrity. Proven ability to interpret complex information, prepare analyses/reports, as they apply to grants/funding sources, Proven ability to effectively communicate with all levels of staff, and agencies, advocacy groups, providers, and the public at large using communication styles appropriate to the audience Proven ability to lead, supervise, direct assign, and evaluate the work of subordinates, the proven ability to communicate effectively. Proven ability to work effectively as a member of the leadership team. Proven ability to meet and conform to the requirements of an operational set of performance specifications, and related capacities and abilities. Required Qualifications Education: Master\u2019s degree in Public Administration, Management, Education, Psychology or in the specifically assigned area of organizational or program responsibility supplemented by extensive specialized or advanced training or education in that area. Experience : \u2022 A minimum of three years of program administrative experience in the area of intellectual and developmental disabilities. \u2022 Experience managing budgets and contracts and a proven ability to develop collaborations and engage with multiple stakeholders as well as experience with grant funding. Preferred Qualifications \u2022 Ph.D. in Public Administration, Management, Education, Psychology \u2022 Work or life experience with individuals with disabilities. \u2022 Experience providing technical assistance to projects. Does this position have Direct Reports? Yes Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 15NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $90,000-$95,000 Work Schedule 35 Hours Monday through Friday Non standard work hours Including some evenings and weekends. Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Executive Director of Sherlock Center on Disabilities Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Grant-funded End of Temporary or Limited Position 06/30/2027 Collective Bargaining Unit Non-union Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 02/26/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD or master\u2019s degree in public administration, Management, Education, Psychology? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of three years of program administrative experience in the area of intellectual and developmental disabilities? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11381": {"title": "Locksmith I", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Locksmith I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Locksmith I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Information Position Information Posting Number CS00647 Position Title Locksmith I Division Administration and Finance Division Department Name Physical Plant Administration Position Type Staff \u2013 Classified General Statement of Duties To perform skilled work involving the installation, repair and maintenance of locks and access systems; and to do related work as required. Supervision Received Works under the general supervision of the superior from whom work assignments are received with latitude for the exercise of initiative; work is reviewed for results and conformance to policies, procedures and instructions. Supervision Exercised As required, supervises the work of trades people assigned to assist in the installation, maintenance and repair of locks and access systems. Position Overview The Locksmith I installs, repairs, and maintains mechanical, electronic, and computerized locks and access control systems to support secure and reliable facility access. Working under general supervision, the role troubleshoots lock and card access issues, programs and audits access systems, maintains related wiring and power supplies, coordinates preventive maintenance, manages supplies and equipment, and prepares reports. The position may supervise assisting tradespeople and requires journeyman locksmith experience, knowledge of computerized security systems, and relevant education or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Illustrative Examples of Work Performed To perform skilled work involving the installation, repair and maintenance of locks and access systems. To be responsible for the installation and maintenance of all access systems, included but not limited to mechanical, electronic and computerized locks and locking systems. To operate computer programs and databases specifically designed to operate, program and audit computer managed access systems. To install and maintain electronic locks; to program and repair Card Access Control systems that provide access; to diagnose problems that arise concerning outside doors not unlocking Card Access controllers not operating, card swipes not working, communication problems involving computer modems. To install electronic magnets on perimeter doors and maintain the wiring and power supplies that controls them. To develop preventive maintenance schedules and apply them to the activities of the staff. To maintain an inventory of necessary supplies and equipment and requisition supplies and equipment as needed. To be responsible for the equipment, materials, tools, and supplies necessary for proper installation, maintenance and repair. To submit written recommendations and reports as required. To do related work as required. Education Such as may have been gained through: graduation from a senior high school, in addition, up to date seminar and computer course work on IBM and MAC programming. Experience Such as may have been gained through: experience working with computer/software applications, plus journeyman locksmith experience. Or Combination of Education and Experience Any combination of education and experience that shall be substantially equivalent to the above education and experience. Additional Required Qualifications Knowledges Skills and Capacities A thorough knowledge of the practices, processes, tools and materials utilized in the installation, maintenance and repair of all mechanical, electronic and computerized security locking system; the ability to analyze programming and mechanical breakdowns and take appropriate corrective action, including the procurement of materials or services; a working knowledge of computers, computer hardware, and all peripherals associated with the daily operation computers; and related capacities and abilities. Preferred Qualifications Experience installing, programming, and troubleshooting electronic locks and card access control systems. Experience managing access control software and databases, including access permissions and system audits. Skill in diagnosing problems with door hardware, electromagnetic locks, wiring, power supplies, and communications equipment. Experience developing preventive maintenance schedules and maintaining tools, equipment, and supply inventories. Experience coordinating or supervising tradespeople on installation and repair projects. Strong customer service, communication, and documentation skills. Completion of relevant locksmith or access control training or certifications. Position Details FLSA Non-Exempt Full Time / Part Time Full-time Work Schedule Full-Time, 40 weekly hours Monday \u2013 Friday 8:00AM \u2013 4:30PM Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Director, Facilities and Operations Position Status Permanent - C End of Restricted or Limited Position Civil Service List No Union Code classified Salary Grade 315CA Minimum Salary for Grade $48,771 Maximum Salary for Grade $53,059 Added Salary for This Position Collective Bargaining Unit Council 94 Local 2878 Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Anticipated Start Date 10/10/2026 Application Open Date Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a High School diploma? Yes No * Do you have computer course work on IBM and MAC programming? Yes No * Do you have experience working with computer/software applications, plus journeyman locksmith experience? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11002": {"title": "Coordinator, RI Vision Education and Services", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Coordinator, RI Vision Education and Services Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Coordinator, RI Vision Education and Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00745 Position Title Coordinator, RI Vision Education and Services Division Academic Affairs Division Department Name Sherlock Center on Disabilities Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview The Paul V. Sherlock Center on Disabilities at Rhode Island College invites applications for the Vision Services Coordinator, Paul V. Sherlock Center on Disabilities. The Vision Services Coordinator will coordinate management and administrative activities of the Rhode Island Vision Services Program. The Paul V. Sherlock Center on Disabilities, founded at Rhode Island College in 1993, is a University Center for Excellence in Developmental Disabilities ( UCEDD ). UCEDDs are evidence driven and designed to advance policies, practices and research that improve the health, education, social and economic well-being of people with disabilities, their families, and their communities. The mission of the Sherlock Center is to promote membership of individuals with disabilities in school, work and the community. Primary Purpose The individual will coordinate activities of the Rhode Island Vision Services Program. Essential Duties Develop, maintain and report an accurate census of children (birth-22) who are blind and/or visually impaired in the State of Rhode Island. Develop strategies for continuous tracking of population changes and needs, including the analysis of workloads to ensure proper resource allocation. Coordinate professional development activities for the Rhode Island Teachers of Students with Visual Impairments (TVIs) (and potentially other TVIs employed by agencies other than the state) to effectively meet these needs. Supervise, evaluate, and provide support to the TVIs and Certified Orientation & Mobility Specialists (COMs) using a RIDE approved evaluation system. Develop, implement and evaluate a system for collecting information on the outcomes achieved by children who are blind and/or visually impaired, to evaluate the effectiveness of services and supports. Design, implement and assess a system to link the integration of vision services with the instructional initiatives and standards of local school districts. Serve as the liaison connecting the Rhode Island Department of Education Office of Student, Community, and Academic Support, the Rhode Island Department of Health and Human Services Office of Early Intervention, and the Rhode Island Department of Human Services, Office of Rehabilitation Services, Services for the Blind and Visually Impaired ( SBVI ). Report to the Rhode Island Department of Education Office of Student, Community, and Academic Support, the Rhode Island Department of Health and Human Services Office of Early Intervention, and the Rhode Island Department of Human Services, Office of Rehabilitation Services, Services for the Blind and Visually Impaired ( SBVI ) as required by them. Identify and develop grant proposals to support current and future initiatives. Provide technical assistance to the Rhode Island Department of Education Office of Student, Community and Academic Support as needed, such as addressing the accessibility of state assessments, the certification requirements of TVIs, and other matters as related to students who are blind and/or visually impaired Act as the Ex Officio Trustee and manage the federal quota account and materials as designated by the Rhode Island Department of Education. Develop written policies/procedures for the program as applicable Occasional Duties Travel to schools, early intervention sites, community sites, and other agencies as needed. Provide professional development to various service providers. Provide community outreach. Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Director, Paul V. Sherlock Center on Disabilities Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Knowledge of Early Intervention and Special Education systems in Rhode Island. Knowledge of the RI Teacher Evaluation System Knowledge of federal and state laws and regulations pertaining to special education. Knowledge of research about best practices for educating children who are blind and/or visually impaired. Knowledge of strategies for assessing the programmatic needs of children who are blind and/or visually impaired. Knowledge of strategies for monitoring the effectiveness of programs. Ability to collaborate with professionals and families. Effective communication skills \u2013 oral and written Familiarity with Education Union Contracts Ability to manage electronic data using databases and spreadsheets Excellent organizational skills Understanding of school systems including educational programs for students, data collection, and organization structure and function Understanding of the sensitivity of information and the ability to handle confidential information Establish and maintain effective working relationships Required Qualifications Education : Master\u2019s Degree in a discipline related to education and a valid RI Building Administrator and/or District Level Administrator: Special Education Certification. Experience in needs assessment, outcome measurement, and evaluation of teachers working with special populations. In lieu of an administrative certificate, candidate has a minimum of three years\u2019 experience implementing and managing programs of children with Special Education Needs, as well as knowledge of state and federal special education laws, regulations, and policies. This may include serving as an LEA at the building level and/or providing technical assistance to districts, programs and teachers. Preferred Qualifications Experience as a District Level Special Education Administrator and/or approved RI Department of Education Teacher Evaluator. Does this position have Direct Reports? No Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 12NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $85,000 - $90,000 Work Schedule Full Time, 35 hours per week Benefits Full-time employee benefits include: Comprehensive Health Benefits and Rewards for Wellness Incentives Generous Paid Time Off Family/Parental Leave Tuition Waivers at RIC , CCRI & URI Retirement Plan Long-term Disability Coverage Variety of voluntary add-on\u2019s For a complete listing, visit: http://www.employeebenefits.ri.gov/benefits/new/index.php Reports To (Title) Director, Paul V. Sherlock Center on Disabilities Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Grant-funded End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit Non-union Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 06/12/2025 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master\u2019s Degree in a discipline related to education? Yes No * Do you have experience as a District Level Special Education Administrator and/or approved RI Department of Education Teacher Evaluator? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts 2 Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/10366": {"title": "Foreign Language Instructor", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Foreign Language Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Foreign Language Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Positions are contingent upon the level of federal funding and student enrollment. Salary range: $2,800 to $3,500. The salary may be adjusted based on student enrollment. Candidates are required to upload a resume and cover letter. In the cover letter, please indicate the high school level course(s) the candidate is applying to teach: Arabic, German, Japanese, Korean, Mandarin Chinese, or Modern Greek. Provide the names and contact information for three current professional references. At least one reference must come from an educational administrator who has supervised the applicant. Please include the title of each person providing a reference. Taxes will be withheld from the salary, and payment will be made on August 7th. No fringe benefits will be provided. Attention foreign citizens working in the U.S. under a visa: This position is short-term, and Rhode Island College will not sponsor a work authorization visa. Before finalizing employment, this position requires successful completion of a background check, which may include, but is not limited to, verification of education, employment history, and a criminal and sex offender record check. The employee must also submit specific forms required by the RI College Human Resources Office as outlined in the terms. Posting Details Posting Detail Information Posting Number NT00125 Position Title/Assigment Foreign Language Instructor Department Name Position Type Staff - Casual Position Description Posting Information Number of Positions Available Benefits Eligible? No Application Open Date 02/18/2026 Additional Information Positions are contingent upon the level of federal funding and student enrollment. Salary range: $2,800 to $3,500. The salary may be adjusted based on student enrollment. Candidates are required to upload a resume and cover letter. In the cover letter, please indicate the high school level course(s) the candidate is applying to teach: Arabic, German, Japanese, Korean, Mandarin Chinese, or Modern Greek. Provide the names and contact information for three current professional references. At least one reference must come from an educational administrator who has supervised the applicant. Please include the title of each person providing a reference. Taxes will be withheld from the salary, and payment will be made on August 7th. No fringe benefits will be provided. Attention foreign citizens working in the U.S. under a visa: This position is short-term, and Rhode Island College will not sponsor a work authorization visa. Before finalizing employment, this position requires successful completion of a background check, which may include, but is not limited to, verification of education, employment history, and a criminal and sex offender record check. The employee must also submit specific forms required by the RI College Human Resources Office as outlined in the terms. EEO Statement As an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity institution that values and is committed to inclusion and expanding the diversity of its faculty and staff, the College invites members of protected classes, including minorities and persons with disabilities, to identify themselves as such at the time of application. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * 1. * Are you available to meet the required time commitments set forth in this summer job description? yes no * Have you taught this subject for at least 2 years to groups of low-income, first-generation high school students in a formal classroom setting, with at least fifteen students in each group? Yes No * Have you at least 2 years of experience developing course curriculum and learning objectives aligned to Common Core/State Standards? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document (see special instructions) Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11370": {"title": "Manager, User Support Services, Customer Support", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Manager, User Support Services, Customer Support Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Manager, User Support Services, Customer Support Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00893 Position Title Manager, User Support Services, Customer Support Division Administration and Finance Division Department Name User Support Services Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview The Manager, User Support Services, Customer Support helps students, faculty, and staff at Rhode Island College make effective use of the technology that supports learning, teaching, and daily work. Leading the IT Help Center\u2019s staff and student assistants, this role oversees technical support, computer services, and audiovisual equipment for classrooms and campus events. The manager coordinates timely responses to technology needs, guides staff training, and plans equipment upgrades and replacements. Through collaboration across IT and the campus community, the position improves support services and helps shape future technology investments. Primary Purpose The Manager of User Support Services (Customer Support), will plan and manage technology, college applications and customer support methodologies in support of business office productivity, student learning and faculty teaching tools. The individual will also manage the operation and staff of the IT Help Center for media and client technology distribution; oversee the operation of help desk technology services and customer support, and the distribution and service of client technologies, classroom media, and audio/video equipment. Essential Duties Provide leadership and supervision to the Help Center support team consisting of full-time staff and student support. Coordinate with other areas of the Information Technology Services department as necessary. Plan and manage the day-to-day operation of the help desk and media and technology services. Manage the recruitment, scheduling, training and supervision of IT Help Center staff and student assistants. Plan and manage installation, repair and maintenance of desktop and mobile computers and peripherals. Provide strategic, budget/fiscal and technology planning for instructional support initiatives. Manage distribution and end-user support of audio, video, and multimedia equipment in classrooms and during campus events. Oversee and schedule the systematic replacement cycle for computer hardware, peripherals and audiovisual equipment. Evaluate and analyze customer requirements for services. Maintain an accurate and up-to-date inventory of hardware, software, vendor warranties and licensing agreements. Maintain and configure application software for help desk/audiovisual services management (e.g. call center/help desk tracking system, audiovisual scheduling, system configuration, remote access, asset mangement, etc). Utilize system tools for data analysis and reporting. Coordinate training for Information Services staff for help desk and audiovisual system software for help desk ticketing, asset management, etc. Monitor the status of all help desk tickets and coordinate with other groups within Information Services to ensure that end user requests are answered and/or forwarded to an appropriate staff member. Provide basic end user support for supported software applications. Develop and maintain documentation. Provide distribution, consultation and troubleshooting for hardware and software problems related to computer hardware, peripherals, audio, video, videoconferencing and multimedia equipment and software. Participate in college committees and working groups to promote best practice use of information technology in administration and instruction. Perform the duties of a Lead Information Technologist. Occasional Duties Stay abreast of advances in technology for help desk and audiovisual hardware, software and services. Work with vendors and other outside companies and agencies as needed. Perform other related duties as requested by the Director of User Support Services. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities In-depth knowledge of application software and hardware used to support a college environment. Ability to organize, coordinate & direct and assess support staff. Ability to interpret institutional policies, plans, objectives, rules and regulations and communicate the interpretation to others. Ability to communicate effectively (verbally and in writing) and possess strong interpersonal skills. Demonstrated continuous professional development. Strong customer service skills. Technical and interpersonal problem-solving skills. Ability to translate concepts into technical solutions. Demonstrated understanding of the workflow and process requirements of business units related to applications. Demonstrated ability to provide outstanding customer service, be a good listener and work well with a diverse group of customers and IT. Demonstrated ability to be the subject matter expert in supporting, maintaining, and administering complex applications. Excellent problem solving/analytical skills, knowledge of analytical tools, and complex troubleshooting methods. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor\u2019s degree. Experience: Six years\u2019 experience working at a mid-to-large size information technology help desk including two years of experience in either of the following areas: overseeing or coordinating the activities of help desk staff; or serving as a project lead for major help desk initiatives. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in CS, CIS , Engineering, or related discipline. Appropriate industry certifications. Significant team leadership and/or supervisory experience in information technology. Bilingual. Does this position have Direct Reports? Yes Environmental Conditions This position requires frequent lifting, moving, and/or installation of moderately heavy equipment (such as computers), audiovisual equipment, wiring and related work. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 15NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $105,000 - $115,000 Work Schedule Full-Time, 35 hours per week. Monday \u2013 Friday 8:30AM \u2013 4:30PM May be required to work outside of normal business hours based on departmental needs. Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Director, User Support Services Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Continuing End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit PSA Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 10/01/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor's degree? Yes No * Do you have six years of experience working at a mid-to-large size information technology help desk including two years of experience in either of the following areas: overseeing or coordinating the activities of help desk staff; or serving as a project lead for major help desk initiatives? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11331": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty Positions Academic Year 2026", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty Positions Academic Year 2026 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjunct Faculty Positions Academic Year 2026 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC/AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld. There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis as needs arise within departments. Candidates will be contacted if an opportunity aligns with their qualifications. Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1,683/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjunct Faculty Positions Academic Year 2026 Department Name Academic Affairs Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Other Position Overview Rhode Island College is creating a pool of qualified candidates for potential adjunct faculty positions across various departments, including but not limited to Biology, Chemistry, English, First Year Writing, Mathematics, Modern Languages, Political Science, Psychology. We seek dedicated and dynamic educators who are passionate about teaching and committed to fostering a positive learning environment for our diverse student body. PLEASE DO NOT APPLY TO THIS JOB POSTING , APPLICATIONS WILL ONLY BE ACCEPTED THROUGH THE DEPARTMENT AD LINKS BELOW Available Positions (Click on below links to apply): Adjunct Faculty, Modern Languages Adjunct Faculty, English Adjunct Faculty, Psychology Adjunct Faculty, First-Year Writing Adjunct Faculty, Biology (Introductory) Adjunct Faculty, Biology (Anatomy and Physiology) Adjunct Faculty, Political Science Adjunct Faculty, Mathematics Adjunct Faculty, Chemistry Essential Duties Occasional Duties Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Qualifications Preferred Qualifications Environmental Conditions Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00040 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available Multiple Anticipated Start Date or Semester Fall 2026 Semester Posting Date 10/31/2024 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC / AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld. There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis as needs arise within departments. Candidates will be contacted if an opportunity aligns with their qualifications. Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How long have you been employed in your current classification? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11326": {"title": "Adjuncts, Biology Department (Microbiology) (2026)", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjuncts, Biology Department (Microbiology) (2026) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjuncts, Biology Department (Microbiology) (2026) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position Union eligibility: Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC/AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld There are no fringe benefits with this position Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available. Writing sample, teaching evaluations, and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1,683/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjuncts, Biology Department (Microbiology) (2026) Department Name Biology Department Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Faculty of Arts and Science Position Overview The Biology Department is seeking candidates to fill part-time instructor positions with expertise in Microbiology and Bacteriology. We welcome applications from those qualified to teach introductory, intermediate, and advanced courses. We seek adjunct faculty committed to teaching and working with our multicultural student population, teaching courses as needed at the undergraduate/graduate level. Essential Duties Teach in-person specialty classes populated by students majoring in the following areas: Biology, Health Sciences, Nursing. Occasional Duties Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in a biological science. Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate instruction and to mentoring students. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching introductory biology and advanced courses including microbiology lecture and laboratory. Experience with nontraditional students and with an ethnically diverse student population. Environmental Conditions Teaching/instruction is performed in a traditional classroom setting. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00057 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available Multiple Anticipated Start Date or Semester Fall 2026 Posting Date 10/27/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position Union eligibility: Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC / AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld There are no fringe benefits with this position Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available. Writing sample, teaching evaluations, and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11409": {"title": "Higher Education Administrative Assistant III", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Higher Education Administrative Assistant III Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Higher Education Administrative Assistant III Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates selected for further consideration may be required to complete a practical exercise. The exercise is a candidate screening tool that may be used to assess computer software skills specific to the job. Examples include but are not limited to Microsoft Word (mail merge, formatting, etc.), Microsoft Excel (charts, tables, formulas, etc.), and typing. Upon hire, candidate may be required to arrange for an official transcript of highest degree earned to be mailed/transmitted directly from the institution to RIC. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Information Position Information Posting Number CS00649 Position Title Higher Education Administrative Assistant III Division Academic Affairs Division Department Name Feinstein School of Education and Human Development Position Type Staff \u2013 Classified General Statement of Duties Within a college/university system, to assist in the organization and maintenance of a wide variety of complex academic programs and services by performing complex administrative support functions; to utilize college enterprise software systems with common business applications and a wide variety of computer applications including word processing, spreadsheets and other contemporary office software; and to do related work as required. Supervision Received Works under the general supervision of an academic department chair, Dean, faculty or other designated academic professional; work instructions are typically provided at the beginning of assignments and is subject to episodic review by a supervisor for conformance with such policies, procedures and methods. Supervision Exercised To serve in an advisory or consulting capacity to Higher Education Administrative Assistant I\u2019s and II\u2019s or other staff assigned; As assigned by a superior, to supervise, provide guidance to, be a resource for and review the work of Higher Education Assistant I\u2019s and II\u2019s, or other assigned staff. Position Overview The Higher Education Administrative Assistant III provides advanced administrative and operational support to the Feinstein School of Education and Human Development, contributing to the effective delivery of academic programs and services. Working closely with faculty, staff, and students, this position coordinates school activities, maintains academic and research records, prepares reports, and facilitates access to campus resources. The role also supports grants and financial processes, reviews transactions, monitors expenditures, coordinates purchasing and inventory, and processes student work-study payroll information. Using college enterprise systems, the position supports accurate reporting, efficient operations, and compliance with institutional and state requirements. This position offers an opportunity to contribute to the work of the Feinstein School of Education and Human Development while applying strong organizational, communication, and problem-solving skills. Illustrative Examples of Work Performed Within a college/university system, to assist in the organization and maintenance of a wide variety of complex academic programs and services by performing complex administrative support functions. To utilize college enterprise software systems with common business applications and a wide variety of computer applications including word processing, spreadsheets and other contemporary office software. To perform advanced clerical support functions in connection with grants and other financial endeavors within an academic department. To provide a high level of complex clerical support, including the maintenance of research/project files within an academic department. To pre-audit and/or post financial information to an integrated financial system after first determining the accuracy and appropriateness of financial transactions within an academic department; to make recommendations regarding the nature/scope of this data. To oversee the operations of department-specific programs. To be responsible for the requisition, inventory, distribution and control of supplies for the department(s), and to ensure compliance with State and college/university purchasing rules and regulations. To coordinate with faculty within the academic department to arrange for any special services required by students, such as referrals for research, tutoring, disability services, Writing Center, English as a Second Language programs, Career Development etc. To gather and prepare academic and statistical reports incorporating information from the data management system to track expenditures, grade point averages, grades, academic probation, etc. To create and manipulate advanced queries within the college\u2019s enterprise software system such as class rosters, academic transcripts, faculty load reports. To make classroom reservations utilizing the college\u2019s event management computer system. To convey pertinent information to faculty, staff, students and visitors within an academic department. To enter hours worked for the biweekly work study student payroll for the academic department. To maintain electronic and/or paper records for the academic department. To schedule faculty advising appointments for students, as well as other events for the academic department chair and faculty. To maintain and requisitions department supplies utilizing the college\u2019s enterprise software system in compliance with college and state purchasing protocols. As assigned by a superior, to manage a P-Card and Travel Card as part of the Purchasing/Budgeting process in the department. To produce and present detailed reports on departmental key performance indicators. To develop and maintain policies and procedures for the academic department. To do related work as required. Education Such as may have been gained through: graduation from a senior high school supplemented with college courses in computer information systems. Experience Such as may have been gained through: employment in performing general office tasks of a complex nature in an academic setting, including the use of enterprise software systems with common business applications, word processing, spreadsheets, and other contemporary office software. Or Combination of Education and Experience Any combination of education and experience that shall be substantially equivalent to the above education and experience. Additional Required Qualifications Knowledges Skills and Capacities The ability to integrate information from one type of application package to another; Excellent oral and written communication skills and interpersonal skills; the ability to effectively communicate information to all interested parties within a higher education setting; skills in organizing and multi-tasking; strong written and verbal communication skills; a working knowledge of office practices and the ability to apply such knowledge in recommending improvements in office procedures, use of forms, and the establishment and retention of relevant office records and files; a familiarity with spreadsheets, databases, word processing and other computer software; the ability to organize departmental activities; the ability to work independently as well as part of a team; the ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with superiors, the college/university departments, and other state and private agencies and organizations and employees; the ability to handle multiple tasks quickly with attention to detail; the ability to handle and maintain confidential matters; a working knowledge of a higher education system; the ability to generate accurate and concise informational and statistical reports; and related capacities and abilities. Preferred Qualifications Associate\u2019s degree in Business, or related field. Experience working in a college setting. Position Details FLSA Non-Exempt Full Time / Part Time Full-time Work Schedule Full-Time, 35 Weekly Hours Monday \u2013 Friday 8:30AM \u2013 4:30PM Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Dean, Feinstein School of Education and Human Development Position Status Restricted - C End of Restricted or Limited Position 05/01/2026 Civil Service List No Union Code classified Salary Grade 317CA Minimum Salary for Grade $50,915 Maximum Salary for Grade $55,777 Added Salary for This Position Collective Bargaining Unit Council 94 Local 2879 Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Anticipated Start Date 10/24/2026 Application Open Date Application Close Date 11/05/2026 Special Instructions Candidates selected for further consideration may be required to complete a practical exercise. The exercise is a candidate screening tool that may be used to assess computer software skills specific to the job. Examples include but are not limited to Microsoft Word (mail merge, formatting, etc.), Microsoft Excel (charts, tables, formulas, etc.), and typing. Upon hire, candidate may be required to arrange for an official transcript of highest degree earned to be mailed/transmitted directly from the institution to RIC . Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11403": {"title": "Director, Dining and Retail Food Services", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Director, Dining and Retail Food Services Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Director, Dining and Retail Food Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please upload a copy of your current RI Department of Health Food Safety Manager Certification. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00899 Position Title Director, Dining and Retail Food Services Division Administration and Finance Division Department Name Dining Services Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview The Director of Dining and Retail Food Services provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for Rhode Island College\u2019s comprehensive dining and retail food service program, including campus dining, caf\u00e9s, catering, meal plans, convenience retail, vending, and special event concessions. The Director oversees financial planning, purchasing, personnel management, staff development, facilities planning, and food safety compliance while delivering high-quality, customer-focused services that meet the diverse nutritional and dietary needs of the College community. As the College\u2019s primary resource on food and hospitality services, the Director advances innovative, financially responsible programs that enhance the campus experience, support student success, and align with the College\u2019s mission and strategic goals. Primary Purpose The Director of Dining and Retail Food Services is responsible for the efficient and effective administration of all aspects of the dining and retail food operations; serving as the primary source of campus expertise on food and hospitality services; providing vision and leadership in the development of a comprehensive, campus wide food service program which consistently meets the needs and expectations of a diverse college community, while attaining required financial objectives; responsible for establishing and fostering foodservice environments which are aligned with, and contribute to the College\u2019s Strategic Plan, Mission, and Goals. Essential Duties Responsible for developing a comprehensive food service program for a diverse college community, as well as the vision, goals and leadership for successful attainment. Responsible for the management and operations of all Dining Service operations to include Donovan Dining Center, The Beestro Cafe, Catering Services, Vending Services (Managed by a 3rd Party), Mobile and Special Event Concessions, Quick Mart Convenience Store and retail operations as maybe assigned. Responsible for the administration of all Dining Service program components to include Meal Plan Programs, Cash Sales, Catering, retail operations, nutritional services, and Conference and Special Events. Provides leadership in the formation of policies, procedures and operational guidelines for Dining Service with a focus on customer service and student success, while ensuring adherence to applicable standards and budgetary objectives. Responsible for the development and implementation of marketing concepts, services, menus, and pricing guidelines which meet the need and expectations of the College community and positively influence customer satisfaction. Responsible for the development of a Nutritional/Dietary Services program component, supporting the unique and diverse needs of the College community. Responsible for the management and oversight of more than 75, management, administrative support, food service, and housekeeping personnel. Responsible for the identification of workforce needs department-wide, development of job assignments, and plan and direct work of assigned employees in a manner which improves operational effectiveness, customer service, and budgetary objectives. Responsible to implement personnel policies for the department, recommend personnel actions and actively participate in labor relation matters to include all levels of the grievance process. Responsible for the development of a highly proficient, professional, and customer centric work force through leadership and training in key areas including but not limited to food preparation, customer service, sanitation, and safety, etc. Prepare, administer, and monitor annual operating budget(s); prepare timely cost accounting reports analyzing the budget status and implement operational changes to achieve efficiencies and attain budgetary goals. Create and/or monitor computerized sales, menu planning, purchasing, inventory, recipe development, payment and accounting systems to insure operational effectiveness. Establish purchasing standards and procedures for the department and oversee the procurement processes for all College Dining Services food and non-food purchases, ensuring the appropriate integrity and efficiencies. Identify and plan for short and long term renovation, maintenance and new equipment needs for Dining Service facilities, prepare related reports, and participate on facilities and building committees. Evaluate, recommend and oversee branded concepts and/or franchise operations campus wide. Advise the Sr. Director od Auxiliary Services & Operations on the matters pertaining to food service. Function as the College\u2019s liaison for food service information and nutritional needs for students, faculty, staff, guests and other state departments. Serve as the primary designated school official for the USDA Federal Commodities Program, State of RI Food Advisory Panel, the RIDOA Prime Vendor Working Group, and the RIC Food Advisory Committee. Exhibit a commitment to professional growth and development through internal and external associations and committees. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Executive Director of Auxiliary Services and Operations. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Demonstrated knowledge of state purchasing procedures, federal and state health laws. Working knowledge of computerized menu management, access and inventory systems. Working knowledge of computerized ID systems. Working knowledge of computerized financial and personnel systems. Be creative and innovative in thinking and work habits, with a commitment to diversity, customer service, and student success. Proficient with personal computers, printers; word processing, database management and spreadsheet software, including Microsoft Office Systems, CBORD Menu Management System, VISIX , PEOPLESOFT , and POS systems. Ability to represent the College positively and effectively with prospective and current students, faculty, staff, alumni, outside agencies and the public. Ability to provide strong leadership and a clear vision to staff, as well as implement policies and procedures with a focus on customer service and student success. Ability and willingness to develop, maintain, and facilitate professional relationships with all internal and external stakeholders. Ability to effectively organize, prioritize, and multi-task in a high volume, fast paced, fluid environment. Possess and demonstrate excellent interpersonal, analytical, and written/oral communication skills. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Business Administration, Public Administration, or related area. Experience: A minimum of ten years of progressively responsible experience in the management of a large, complex, high-volume food service operation. Demonstrated experience in labor relations, staff development and oversight of more than 50 unionized personnel. Demonstrated experience in renovations, and maintenance related to food service facilities. Demonstrated financial experience successfully administering a budget exceeding 8 million dollars in revenue. Licenses / Certifications Possess and maintain a current RI Department of Health Food Safety Manager Certification. Possess and maintain a valid Driver\u2019s License. Preferred Qualifications Does this position have Direct Reports? Yes Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 16NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $95,000 - $125,000 Work Schedule Full-Time, 35 weekly hours Flexible to meet departmental needs. Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Executive Director of Auxiliary Services and Operations Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Continuing End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit PSA Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 10/16/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please upload a copy of your current RI Department of Health Food Safety Manager Certification. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Business Administration, Public Administration, or related area? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of ten years of progressively responsible experience in the management of a large, complex, high-volume food service operation? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in labor relations, staff development and oversight of more than 50 unionized personnel? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in renovations, and maintenance related to food service facilities? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated financial experience successfully administering a budget exceeding 8 million dollars in revenue? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Document (see special instructions) Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11408": {"title": "Higher Education Administrative Assistant I", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Higher Education Administrative Assistant I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Higher Education Administrative Assistant I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates selected for further consideration may be required to complete a practical exercise. The exercise is a candidate screening tool that may be used to assess computer software skills specific to the job. Examples include but are not limited to Microsoft Word (mail merge, formatting, etc.), Microsoft Excel (charts, tables, formulas, etc.), and typing. Upon hire, candidate may be required to arrange for an official transcript of highest degree earned to be mailed/transmitted directly from the institution to RIC. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Information Position Information Posting Number CS00650 Position Title Higher Education Administrative Assistant I Division President's Office Division Department Name Recreation Center Position Type Staff \u2013 Classified General Statement of Duties Within a college/university system, to perform routine administrative support functions in an academic department utilizing college enterprise software systems with common business applications and a wide variety of office equipment and computer software applications including word processing, spreadsheets and other contemporary office programs and equipment; and to do related work as required. Supervision Received Works under the general supervision of an academic department chair, Dean and/or senior faculty member; specific tasks may be given directly by a variety of professionals; instructions usually are given only at the beginning of assignments involving a new type of work; work is generally in final form when compared and is subject o, but does not always receive, review by supervisors. Supervision Exercised None. Position Overview The Higher Education Administrative Assistant I plays an essential role in supporting the daily operations of an academic department and creating a welcoming, responsive environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Working closely with department leadership and faculty, this position coordinates schedules and appointments, maintains departmental records, prepares correspondence and reports, and uses college software systems to support academic and administrative activities. Responsibilities include assisting students with course requests and information about academic policies and services, arranging classroom reservations and departmental events, supporting work study scheduling and payroll entry, and processing supply requests. The role offers an opportunity to contribute to student success while helping an academic department operate efficiently. An ideal candidate brings strong organizational and communication skills, attention to detail, proficiency with common office software, and the ability to manage varied assignments and build positive working relationships across the college community. Illustrative Examples of Work Performed Within a college/university system, to perform routine administrative support functions in an academic department utilizing college enterprise software systems with common business applications and a wide variety of office equipment and computer software applications including word processing, spreadsheets and other contemporary office programs and equipment. To generate involved statistical statements, reports, legal documents, letters and other materials, utilizing the appropriate office software application, the college\u2019s enterprise software system or from paper copy. To create and manipulate queries within the college\u2019s enterprise software system such as class rosters, academic transcripts, faculty load reports, and other items. to make classroom reservations utilizing the college\u2019s event management system. To convey basic pertinent information to faculty, staff, students and visitors as it relates to a wide range of policies and procedures of the college. To process student add/drop course requests. To coordinate office schedules for work study students within an academic department. To enter hours worked for the biweekly work study student payroll for the academic department. To maintain electronic and/or paper records for the academic department. To answer in-person, telephone or email inquiries for the academic department and respond appropriately. To convey information to students regarding course offerings, courses of study, and academic policies and services. To schedule faculty advising appointments for students as well as other events for the academic department chair and faculty. To maintain and requisition department supplies utilizing the college\u2019s enterprise software system in compliance with college and state purchasing protocols. To perform routine maintenance of office machinery and equipment. To do related work as required. Education Such as may have been gained through: graduation from a senior high school supplemented with training in computer information systems. Experience Such as may have been gained through: employment in performing general office tasks of a complex nature in an academic setting, including the sue of enterprise software systems with common business applications, word processing, spreadsheets, and other contemporary office software. Or Combination of Education and Experience Any combination of education and experience that shall be substantially equivalent to the above education and experience. Additional Required Qualifications Knowledges Skills and Capacities The ability to integrate information from one type of application package to another; the ability to generate accurate and concise written reports; a working knowledge of general office practices, business arithmetic and business English; a familiarity with spreadsheets, databases, word processing and other computer software; the ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with supervisors, the college/university departments, and other state and private agencies and organizations and employees; the ability to understand and carry out complex oral and written instructions; a working knowledge of higher education policies and procedures as well as general office practices; and related capacities and abilities. Preferred Qualifications Position Details FLSA Non-Exempt Full Time / Part Time Part time Work Schedule Part-Time, 19 weekly hours Monday \u2013 Thursday (1:00 PM \u2013 5:00 PM) Friday (1:00 PM \u2013 4:00 PM) Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Assistant Athletic Director for Recreation Position Status Permanent - C End of Restricted or Limited Position Civil Service List No Union Code classified Salary Grade 312CA Minimum Salary for Grade 45,887 Maximum Salary for Grade 49,588 Added Salary for This Position Collective Bargaining Unit Council 94 Local 2879 Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Anticipated Start Date 10/24/2026 Application Open Date Application Close Date 11/05/2026 Special Instructions Candidates selected for further consideration may be required to complete a practical exercise. The exercise is a candidate screening tool that may be used to assess computer software skills specific to the job. Examples include but are not limited to Microsoft Word (mail merge, formatting, etc.), Microsoft Excel (charts, tables, formulas, etc.), and typing. Upon hire, candidate may be required to arrange for an official transcript of highest degree earned to be mailed/transmitted directly from the institution to RIC . Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement As an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity institution which values and is committed to expanding the diversity of its faculty and staff, the College invites members of protected classes, including minorities and persons with disabilities, to identify themselves as such at the time of application. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11410": {"title": "Heavy Motor Equipment Mechanic / Operator", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Heavy Motor Equipment Mechanic / Operator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Heavy Motor Equipment Mechanic / Operator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. At the time of appointment must be physically qualified to perform assigned duties as evidenced by a physician\u2019s certificate. Must possess the proper operator\u2019s license(s) issued in conformance to requirements of the Rhode Island Registry of Motor Vehicles and/or Rhode Island Department of Labor and Training to operate above described equipment, and must maintain such licensure as a condition of employment. Posting Information Position Information Posting Number CS00651 Position Title Heavy Motor Equipment Mechanic / Operator Division Administration and Finance Division Department Name Physical Plant Administration Position Type Staff \u2013 Classified General Statement of Duties To operate, adjust, service and repair a variety of heavy construction and maintenance equipment, except power shovels, such as: graders, bulldozers, road rollers, power sweepers, hydrocranes, front end loaders, and truck and trailer units, etc.; and to do related work as required. Supervision Received Assignments of repair work or construction tasks are issued by a superior; work methods are subject to approval but not constantly supervised; work is subject to review upon completion for satisfactory results and conformity with technical requirements. Supervision Exercised Occasionally, may direct the work of assigned subordinates. Position Overview The Heavy Motor Equipment Mechanic/Operator operates, adjusts, services, and repairs a variety of heavy construction and maintenance equipment, including graders, bulldozers, loaders, sweepers, hydrocranes, and truck and trailer units. The position performs major mechanical repairs, including engine, drivetrain, and front-end replacement; maintains and repairs water lines and systems; and uses heavy equipment to grade, repair, and resurface roads, parking lots, and paths. Working under general supervision, the employee is responsible for assigned equipment, maintains service records and reports, and may occasionally direct assigned staff in skilled maintenance work. Illustrative Examples of Work Performed To operate, adjust, service and maintain a variety of heavy construction and maintenance equipment, such as: graders, bulldozers, front end loaders, power sweepers, hydrocranes, trucks and tractor trailer units, etc. To be responsible for assigned motor equipment, making necessary repairs and maintaining proper servicing. To repair or replace entire engines, drive trains, front ends of heavy equipment, i.e. power sweeps, front end loaders, trucks, four wheel drive off road vehicles. To be responsible for repair and/or replacement of water lines and water systems. To operate heavy equipment in the repair or replacement of the entire surface of parking lots and/or roads damaged from erosion or general use. As required, to operate equipment such as light trucks, compressors, and other light equipment; or to work as a Motor Equipment Operator. To grade all roads, parking lots, paths, with minimal supervision. As required, to supervise subordinates assigned to perform skilled maintenance. To keep records and make written or oral reports. To do related work as required. Education Such as may have been gained through: completion of twelve school grades, including or supplemented by courses in mechanics and vehicle repair. Experience Such as may have been gained through: employment requiring the operation and maintenance of heavy diesel and gasoline motor equipment and trucks dealing with various phases of construction and maintenance. Or Combination of Education and Experience Any combination of education and experience that shall be substantially equivalent to the above education and experience. Additional Required Qualifications Knowledges Skills and Capacities A working knowledge of the methods, practices and tools used in maintaining heavy construction and maintenance equipment; a working knowledge of the methods and practices used in the repair or replacement of water lines and water systems; a working knowledge of the methods and means used to repair or replace the surface of parking lots and roads; the ability to grade roads, parking lots and paths, with minimal supervision; the ability to perform tasks with mechanical aptitude; the ability to understand and follow instructions; the ability to prepare and keep simple records and to make reports; demonstrated ability to repair or replace entire engines, drive trains, and front ends of heavy equipment, i.e. power sweepers, front end loaders, trucks, four wheel drive off road vehicles; and related capacities and abilities. Preferred Qualifications Position Details FLSA Non-Exempt Full Time / Part Time Full-time Work Schedule Full-Time, 40 Weekly Hours Monday \u2013 Friday 7:00 AM \u2013 3:30 PM Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Associate Director of Facilities and Operations, Business Management and Grounds Position Status Permanent - C End of Restricted or Limited Position Civil Service List No Union Code classified Salary Grade 318CA Minimum Salary for Grade $52,062 Maximum Salary for Grade $57,606 Added Salary for This Position Collective Bargaining Unit Council 94 Local 2878 Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Anticipated Start Date 10/24/2026 Application Open Date Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. At the time of appointment must be physically qualified to perform assigned duties as evidenced by a physician\u2019s certificate. Must possess the proper operator\u2019s license(s) issued in conformance to requirements of the Rhode Island Registry of Motor Vehicles and/or Rhode Island Department of Labor and Training to operate above described equipment, and must maintain such licensure as a condition of employment. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11401": {"title": "Assistant to the Director of Athletics", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Assistant to the Director of Athletics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Assistant to the Director of Athletics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00892 Position Title Assistant to the Director of Athletics Division President's Office Division Department Name Athletics and Recreation Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview The Assistant to the Director of Intercollegiate Athletics and Recreation helps shape a positive, engaging experience for student-athletes and the broader campus community. Working closely with the director, this role supports student-athlete success and keeps athletics and recreation programs running smoothly by coordinating student support services, team travel, facilities, and athletic events. The position also contributes to fundraising, community outreach, and marketing, while guiding student-athlete leadership activities and helping build school spirit and fan engagement. Primary Purpose To support the Director of Intercollegiate Athletics and Recreation in the planning, development, implementation, coordination and supervision of programs, and activities that are athletic and recreational in nature with special emphasis on student and student-athlete programming. Essential Duties Assist in the supervision and programming of the Department\u2019s student-athlete support services with ongoing emphasis on student-athlete success and retention (i.e., academic support and counseling, registration, prepare statistical reports, monitor enrollment, etc.). Assist in the overall and safe management of the Recreation Center with specific emphasis on the membership operation including the computation of relevant data (i.e., program attendance, etc.) and the support of ongoing fiscal controls. Assist in the overall and safe management of the Department\u2019s motor pool and transportation operation. Assist and support special community, and campus-based programming (i.e., CHOICES , community service projects, marketing events, summer camps, etc). Assist in departmental fundraising activities with special emphasis in the upgrading and upkeep delivery of an email, web-based, delivery system. Assist in the delivery of services (i.e., prepare purchasing reports, etc.), as well as the maintenance of inventory of the Department\u2019s equipment operation. Assist in contest management to insure a safe, friendly, and professional environment for users and patrons, manage and program in-house ticket production system (i.e., ticket sales, support facility oversight, etc.). Provide oversight with NCAA mandated Student-Athlete Advisory Committee coordinating their activities and meetings. Assist in the management with, and provide ongoing oversight for, the school and clinic program aimed at community outreach and fundraising. Provide daily oversight and be accountable for all completed intercollegiate team travel including reconciliation forms and roster accountability. Assist in the 24/7 management of athletic recreation facilities. Supervision of marketing and promotions\u2019 intern with emphasis directed on on-going student attendance, loyalty rewards program and fan engagement. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Director of Intercollegiate Athletics, and Recreation. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Good interpersonal and communication skills (written and oral). Ability to work with a diversified population. Strong knowledge and ability with computers and web-based programs. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor\u2019s Degree. Experience: At least four years\u2019 experience gained by working in a college or university environment. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s Degree in physical education, recreation, sports administration, or related field. Bilingual. Does this position have Direct Reports? No Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 10NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $60,000 - $66,000 Work Schedule Non-Standard Work Week. Nights and weekends required. Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Director of Athletics and Executive Director of the Anchor Fund Academic or Calendar Year Calendar Position Status Continuing End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit PSA Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 10/02/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor's degree? Yes No * Do you have at least four years of experience gained by working in a college or university environment? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11407": {"title": "Head Coach, Men&#39;s Lacrosse", "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Head Coach, Men&#39;s Lacrosse Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Head Coach, Men's Lacrosse Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number NC00902 Position Title Head Coach, Men's Lacrosse Division President's Office Division Department Name Athletics and Recreation Position Type Staff - Non Classified Position Overview The Men\u2019s Head Lacrosse Coach at Rhode Island College provides leadership and oversight for all aspects of the men\u2019s intercollegiate lacrosse program, including recruiting, practice planning, game strategy, scheduling, and fundraising. Reporting to the Director of Intercollegiate Athletics and Recreation, the coach recruits academically and athletically qualified student-athletes, supports their academic progress, and builds campus partnerships to promote student success. This full-time, academic-year position also contributes to instructional programs, clinics, and departmental fundraising while upholding NCAA rules, regulations, and philosophies. Primary Purpose As Head Coach, this individual is responsible for all aspects of the men\u2019s lacrosse program (recruiting, conducting practices, games\u2019 strategy, scheduling, academic monitoring, fundraising, etc.) Essential Duties Oversee and be responsible for all aspects of the men\u2019s intercollegiate lacrosse program to include, but not be limited to, recruiting, conducting practices, game strategy, scheduling, etc. with special emphasis on the recruitment of athletic and academically qualified student-athletes. Assist in ongoing instructional lacrosse programs and clinics. Assist in departmental fundraising activities and coordinate fundraising activities as they relate to the men\u2019s lacrosse program. Build ongoing relationships with other campus departments to insure the successful outcome of recruiting student-athletes. Assist and support the academic monitoring of student-athletes. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Director of Intercollegiate Athletics, and Recreation. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Excellent communication skills. Ability to interact with a diversified group of constituents. Knowledge of the NCAA ; its rules, regulations and philosophies. Demonstrated ability to recruit student-athletes at the intercollegiate level. Current Driver\u2019s License with no violations. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor\u2019s Degree. Experience: Three years of successful experience coaching at the intercollegiate level with proven ability to recruit qualified student-athletes. Preferred Qualifications Does this position have Direct Reports? No Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Salary Grade 12NC Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Starting Salary Range $55,000 - $60,000 Work Schedule Full-Time, 35 weekly hours Academic Year Appointment Benefits Full-time employees enjoy an array of benefits including: Health and Wellness \u2013 Medical, Dental & Vision Wellness Incentives and Rewards Paid time Off \u2013 Vacation, Sick & Holiday Retirement Benefits Disability and Insurance Benefits Education Benefits \u2013 Tuition waivers for RIC , CCRI & URI For a complete listing, visit Employee Benefits . Reports To (Title) Director of Intercollegiate Athletics and Recreation Academic or Calendar Year Academic Position Status Continuing End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit Non-union Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Open Date 10/23/2026 Application Close Date Special Instructions Please be advised that Rhode Island College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor's degree? Yes No * Do you have 3 years of successful intercollegiate coaching experience and a proven ability to recruit qualified student-athletes? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}}, "rows": {"https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11321": {"school_id": 1271, "posting_url": "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11321", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct, Department of Elementary Education", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Elementary Education", "area_key_words": "Elementary Education", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "07/07/2026", "position_start_date": "07/07/2026"}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11267": {"school_id": 1271, "posting_url": "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11267", "job_title_in_post": "Director of Professional Studies and Continuing Education", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Professional Studies and Continuing Education", "deadline_of_application": "05/11/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11386": {"school_id": 1271, "posting_url": "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11386", "job_title_in_post": "Electrician", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "08/15/2026"}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11149": {"school_id": 1271, "posting_url": "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11149", "job_title_in_post": "Director, Project Management Office", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Division of Administration and Finance", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "08/03/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/10980": {"school_id": 1271, "posting_url": "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/10980", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant/Associate/Professor Operations Management", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_sc